[2026-07-19T12:30:46.361Z] [INFO]         "type": "text",
[2026-07-19T12:30:46.361Z] [INFO]         "text": "# CI/CD Gap Analysis: hive-mind vs js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template\n\nBoth repos share a common ancestry (the template explicitly credits hive-mind case studies), but the template has since hardened several correctness properties that hive-mind never back-ported. Nothing was modified.\n\n## Gap table\n\n| # | Category | Template has | hive-mind has | Risk | Severity |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Job timeouts | `timeout-minutes` on **all 12** release jobs + link job (`release.yml:58,84,101,132,151,195,246,337,382,487,555,600`; `links.yml:34`) | **4 of 22 jobs** have it (only `docker-publish*`, `release.yml:730,881,1124,1271`). `detect-changes`, `lint`, `test-suites`, `test-execution`, `memory-check-linux`, `release`, `instant-release`, `helm-release`, `changeset-pr`, `validate-docs`, `docker-pr-check`, `helm-pr-check` all inherit GitHub's **6-hour** default | false-negative (hung job burns 6h, never surfaces) | **Critical** |\n| 2 | Timeout enforcement test | `tests/ci-timeouts.test.js` asserts exact per-job timeout AND that job list == expected set (so a new job without a timeout fails CI) | none | false-negative (regression undetectable) | **Critical** |\n| 3 | Main-branch concurrency | `cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.ref != 'refs/heads/main' }}` (`release.yml:44`) + dedicated `concurrency: group: main-writer-…, cancel-in-progress: false` on `release` and `instant-release` (`release.yml:383-385, 488-490`) | `cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' }}` (`release.yml:52`) — **inverted**; no `main-writer` group | false-positive + data loss: a second push to main **cancels an in-flight npm publish / version commit** mid-way | **Critical** |\n| 4 | Push-to-main race | `scripts/push-main-with-rebase-retry.sh` (`set -euo pipefail`, pull --rebase + retry), called from `version-and-commit.mjs:264` | `version-and-commit.mjs:219`: bare `await $\\`git push origin main\\`` | false-positive: `command-stream`'s `$` does **not throw on non-zero exit** (hive-mind documents this itself in `publish-failure-classifier.mjs` header). A rejected push → `version_committed=true` → publish of a version never on main | **Critical** |\n| 5 | Post-publish smoke test | `scripts/smoke-test-package.mjs` (541 lines) run after every publish (`release.yml:465`, `:535`) | absent — no verification the published tarball installs/runs | false-positive: broken package ships green | **High** |\n| 6 | Release-needed self-healing | `scripts/check-changesets.mjs` + `check-release-needed.mjs` (`release.yml:425,431`) — checks npm registry, not git tags; re-releases an unpublished version | inline `find .changeset -name \"*.md\" \\| wc -l` (`release.yml:665-671`); no registry check | false-negative: a failed release is silently never retried | **High** |\n| 7 | `check-mjs-syntax.sh` coverage | loops `for dir in src scripts tests` and counts checked files (`scripts/check-mjs-syntax.sh:14-27`) | loops `*.mjs`, `src/*.mjs`, `tests/*.mjs` — **`scripts/` is never syntax-checked**, and `tests/*.mjs` uses bare `node --check` with **no `timeout 10s`** (`scripts/check-mjs-syntax.sh:14-30`) | false-negative (broken release script merges) + hang with no job timeout (compounds #1) | **High** |\n| 8 | Cancellation propagation | `!cancelled()` everywhere (`release.yml:387,251`); documented as rule #14 in `docs/BEST-PRACTICES.md:197-209` | 10 jobs still use `always()` (`release.yml:146,228,254,292,380,456,484,598,631`), incl. `release` at :631 — hive-mind's *own* comment at :42 says this is wrong | false-negative: cancellation does not propagate; jobs keep running after cancel | **High** |\n| 9 | Secrets scanning | `npx secretlint \"**/*\"` step in lint job (`release.yml:227`) + `.secretlintrc.json` | secretlint is in `devDependencies` (`package.json:73-74,83`) but there is **no `.secretlintrc.json`, no npm script, and no CI step**. Documented as principle #11 (`docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md:276-283`) but not implemented | false-negative: leaked credentials merge | **High** |\n| 10 | Duplication threshold | `.jscpd.json` `\"threshold\": 0`, `\"format\": \"console\"` | `\"threshold\": 11` and `\"format\": [\"javascript\"]` — 11% duplication tolerated, and non-JS files silently unscanned | false-negative | **Medium** |\n| 11 | Broken-link CI | `.github/workflows/links.yml` (lychee + `check-web-archive.mjs` fallback + explicit `exit 1` with remediation text) and `.lycheeignore` | no link workflow, no `.lycheeignore` | false-negative: dead docs links | **Medium** |\n| 12 | Action pinning | `actions/checkout@v6`, `actions/setup-node@v6` | `@v5` throughout (16 call sites, `release.yml:66,90,108,113,…`), plus `FORCE_JAVASCRIPT_ACTIONS_TO_NODE24: true` workaround at `release.yml:50` | warning (deprecation notices) | Medium |\n| 13 | Per-test timeout | `node --test --test-timeout=30000`, `bun test --timeout 30000`; documented at `docs/BEST-PRACTICES.md:186-196` | `npm test` → `scripts/run-tests.mjs`; **no timeout logic anywhere in that file** | false-negative: one hung test → 6h job | Medium |\n| 14 | Workflow-property tests | `tests/workflow-reliability.test.js` (actually *evaluates* the `if:` expressions in JS against synthetic `needs` contexts), `tag-prefix.test.js`, `release-badge.test.js`, `docker-publish.test.js`, `setup-buildx-resilient.test.js` | no equivalents; `tests/test-docker-release-order.mjs` is the only static workflow assertion | false-negative: gating-logic regressions unnoticed | Medium |\n| 15 | Matrix breadth | `test` job matrix = 3 runtimes (node/bun/deno) × 3 OS (`release.yml:240-250`) | single `ubuntu-latest`, node only | false-negative: Windows/macOS/bun/deno breakage | Medium |\n| 16 | Required-docs gate | `validate-docs` asserts required files exist and `exit 1` on missing (`release.yml:340-375`) | `validate-docs` runs `tests/docs-validation.mjs` only, and is gated on `docs-changed == 'true'` so it never runs on code-only pushes | false-negative | Low |\n| 17 | Shell strictness | N/A (template has 4 `.sh` files, all `set -euo pipefail`) | 8 of 9 `.sh` files set it, but `scripts/verify-docker-image.sh:58,265` re-enables `set -u` after disabling, and `test-auto-fork-option.sh:18,27,38`, `test-global-commands.sh:20,26`, `verify-log-file-contents.sh:15` pipe test commands to `\\|\\| true` — **failures are swallowed**, these \"tests\" can never fail | false-positive: `test-execution` job green regardless | **High** |\n| 18 | Workflow-level `run:` strictness | neither repo uses `set -euo pipefail` inside `run:` blocks (both rely on Actions' default `bash -e`) | same | — | Info (parity) |\n| 19 | Job-level `permissions` | `example-app.yml:25` sets a top-level restrictive default; every privileged job declares its own | no workflow-level `permissions`; PR-check jobs (`detect-changes`, `lint`, `test-*`) run with the repo default token scope. `cleanup-test-repos.yml` has **no `permissions` and no `timeout-minutes`** and runs `gh auth refresh -s delete_repo` | warning / security | Medium |\n| 20 | Config drift | `.changeset/config.json` `$schema` @3.1.1 | `$schema` @3.0.0 (`.changeset/config.json:2`) | warning | Low |\n| 21 | Docs | `docs/BEST-PRACTICES.md` §13 (timeouts, with a per-job table) and §14 (cancellation) | `docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md` has **no timeout section and no cancellation section** (headings jump 10→11→12); §11 secrets is documented-but-unimplemented (#9) | — | Medium |\n\nNote in hive-mind's favour: `scripts/publish-failure-classifier.mjs` is **stronger** than the template's — it adds `detectPublishFailure()` / `FAILURE_PATTERNS` for content-based detection of `changeset publish` swallowing npm's exit code (issue #2028). The template only has `NON_RETRYABLE_PATTERNS`. That improvement should flow upstream.\n\n## Prioritized fix list\n\n1. **Invert `cancel-in-progress` on main** (`release.yml:52`) and add the `main-writer-${{ github.repository }}-main` / `cancel-in-progress: false` concurrency group to `release` and `instant-release`. Today a rapid second push to main can cancel a publish between `git push` and `npm publish`.\n2. **Replace `git push origin main`** (`version-and-commit.mjs:219`) with a rebase-retry wrapper, and assert the exit code — `command-stream`'s `$` does not throw, so this is a silent-success path in the release job.\n3. **Add `timeout-minutes` to all 22 jobs** (5 for detect/compile/line-limits/version-check/docs, 10 for lint/changeset/tests, 30 for release paths) and port `tests/ci-timeouts.test.js` so the list-equality assertion catches future untimed jobs. Include `cleanup-test-repos.yml`.\n4. **Fix `scripts/check-mjs-syntax.sh`** to cover `scripts/` and to apply `timeout 10s` to the `tests/` loop.\n5. **Remove `|| true` from the CI-invoked verification scripts** (`test-auto-fork-option.sh:18,27,38`, `test-global-commands.sh:20,26`, `verify-log-file-contents.sh:15`) or make the subsequent assertions actually gate on the captured output — as written the `test-execution` job cannot fail from these steps.\n6. **Port `smoke-test-package.mjs` + `check-changesets.mjs` + `check-release-needed.mjs`** into the release/instant-release jobs.\n7. **Wire up secretlint**: add `.secretlintrc.json` and the lint-job step (the dependency is already installed; the doc already promises it).\n8. **Swap remaining `always()` → `!cancelled()`** at `release.yml:146,228,254,292,380,456,484,598,631`.\n9. **Add a global per-test timeout** to `scripts/run-tests.mjs` (`--test-timeout=30000` equivalent).\n10. Lower `.jscpd.json` threshold from 11 toward 0 and restore `\"format\": \"console\"`; bump actions to `@v6` (which also removes the `FORCE_JAVASCRIPT_ACTIONS_TO_NODE24` workaround at `release.yml:50`); port `links.yml` + `.lycheeignore` + `check-web-archive.mjs`; port `workflow-reliability.test.js`; add timeout/cancellation sections to `docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md` (all 4 language variants)."
