[2026-07-19T12:32:53.567Z] [INFO] {
[2026-07-19T12:32:53.567Z] [INFO]   "type": "assistant",
[2026-07-19T12:32:53.567Z] [INFO]   "message": {
[2026-07-19T12:32:53.567Z] [INFO]     "model": "claude-opus-4-8",
[2026-07-19T12:32:53.567Z] [INFO]     "id": "msg_011CdBRJfBQDVQH79wQ8Xegv",
[2026-07-19T12:32:53.567Z] [INFO]     "type": "message",
[2026-07-19T12:32:53.567Z] [INFO]     "role": "assistant",
[2026-07-19T12:32:53.567Z] [INFO]     "content": [
[2026-07-19T12:32:53.567Z] [INFO]       {
[2026-07-19T12:32:53.567Z] [INFO]         "type": "text",
[2026-07-19T12:32:53.567Z] [INFO]         "text": "I have everything I need. Here is the complete inventory.\n\n---\n\n# CI Log Audit — \"Checks and release\" workflow\n\n**Logs analyzed**\n- `run-29647956700-success.log` (49,914 lines, GREEN, release of `2.8.3`, 16 jobs)\n- `run-29125268021-failure.log` (31,365 lines, RED, 8 jobs — PR-only, no release/docker jobs)\n\nNote: the `<step>` column is `UNKNOWN STEP` for every line in both exports, so step attribution below was reconstructed from the nearest preceding `##[group]Run …` marker.\n\n**Headline:** the build is genuinely green — I found **no hidden test failures**. Every one of the ~180 `N passed, M failed` lines has `M = 0`, and none of the `|| true` sites mask a real regression. The two things that actually deserve action are the **npm publish double-publish race** and the **593 wasted Sentry sourcemap warnings**.\n\n---\n\n## SEVERITY 1 — Real problems that did not fail the build\n\n### 1.1 npm publish runs twice and hard-errors on attempt 2 (publish race)\n- **Job/step:** `Release` / `node scripts/publish-to-npm.mjs --should-pull`\n- **Lines:** 35450–35545 (success log)\n- **Occurrences:** 1 sequence — 2× `npm error code E404` blocks, 1× publish failure, 3 publish attempts\n- **Classification:** REAL-FAILURE-IGNORED (recovered, but the failure is real and wasteful)\n\n```\nPublish attempt 1 of 3...\n🦋  success packages published successfully:\n🦋  @link-assistant/hive-mind@2.8.3\nPublish command reported success; verifying @link-assistant/hive-mind@2.8.3 on npm...\nnpm error code E404\nnpm error 404 No match found for version 2.8.3\nWARNING: post-publish verification failed: version not found on npm\nWaiting 10s before retry...\nPublish attempt 2 of 3...\n🦋  error npm error You cannot publish over the previously published versions: 2.8.3.\n🦋  error packages failed to publish:\nPublish attempt 2 failed: exit code 1\n```\n\n**Root cause:** attempt 1 *did* succeed and created tag `v2.8.3`. `scripts/publish-to-npm.mjs` then verifies with `npm view` immediately (~0.02s later), and the npm registry read replica has not caught up — classic read-after-write propagation lag. The verifier treats E404 as \"publish failed\" and retries. Attempt 2 re-publishes an already-published version and legitimately fails. Attempt 3 finally sees the version live and reports success.\n\nThe green result is luck of the 3-attempt budget: if propagation exceeded ~30s, the job would fail *after* a successful publish and a pushed git tag, leaving the repo in a half-released state. The fix is to make the post-publish verification poll with backoff (and treat \"cannot publish over previously published version\" as *success*, not failure) rather than re-invoking `changeset publish`.\n\n### 1.2 `npm warn publish \"bin[…]\" script name … was invalid and removed` (×10 bins)\n- **Job/step:** `Release` / `publish-to-npm.mjs` (surfaced at lines 35528–35538, inside attempt 2's error dump)\n- **Occurrences:** 10 distinct bin entries, per publish attempt\n- **Classification:** REAL-WARNING-TO-FIX\n\n```\nnpm warn publish npm auto-corrected some errors in your package.json when publishing.  Please run \"npm pkg fix\" to address these.\nnpm warn publish errors corrected:\nnpm warn publish \"bin[hive]\" script name src/hive.mjs was invalid and removed\nnpm warn publish \"bin[solve]\" script name src/solve.mjs was invalid and removed\n… (task, fix, hive-cleanup, review, configure-claude, start-screen, hive-screens, hive-telegram-bot)\n```\n\n**Root cause:** `package.json` `bin` values are `\"./src/hive.mjs\"` etc. npm normalizes/strips these on publish. This is only visible in the log *by accident* — changeset dumps npm's stderr only when the publish command fails, so on a clean single-attempt release this warning is silently swallowed. It affects the published artifact's `bin` map. Fix: run `npm pkg fix` / drop the `./` prefix.\n\n### 1.3 593 Sentry \"could not determine a source map reference\" warnings\n- **Job/step:** `Release` / `echo \"Uploading source maps to Sentry for published packages…\"` → `node scripts/upload-sourcemaps.mjs`\n- **Lines:** 36416–37616 (contiguous); summary headers at 36399 (`Found 236 files`) and 36887 (`Found 357 files`)\n- **Occurrences:** **593** = 236 (`./src`) + 357 (`./tests`), one per file\n- **Classification:** BENIGN-NOISE (functionally a no-op) — but it makes 1,200 log lines of pure noise and the feature it claims to provide does not work\n\n```\n    ~/src/agent-commander.lib.mjs (no sourcemap found)\n      - warning: could not determine a source map reference (Could not auto-detect referenced sourcemap for ~/src/agent-commander.lib.mjs)\n```\n\n**Root cause (confirmed in `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784463865325/scripts/upload-sourcemaps.mjs`):** the script calls\n\n```\nnpx @sentry/cli sourcemaps upload ./src  --release $V --url-prefix '~/src'\nnpx @sentry/cli sourcemaps upload ./tests --release $V --url-prefix '~/tests'\n```\n\n**This project has no build/transpile step.** `package.json`'s `build:pre` is only `chmod +x src/*.mjs` — the shipped artifact *is* the raw `.mjs` source. So there are no `.map` files and no `//# sourceMappingURL=` comments anywhere, and `sentry-cli` warns once per scanned file. Sentry receives the sources (which is mildly useful for stack-frame display) but zero sourcemaps, which is the entire point of the step.\n\nAlso note the script uploads the **357 test files** to Sentry on every release — those can never appear in a production stack trace.\n\nFix options: drop the `./tests` upload; and either delete the sourcemap step (nothing to map) or keep it as a plain source upload while suppressing the warning class. Do not \"fix\" it by generating maps unless a bundler is actually introduced.\n\n### 1.4 jscpd duplication is at 10.61% against a threshold of 11 — 0.39pp of headroom\n- **Job/step:** `lint` / `echo \"Running jscpd code duplication detection…\"` → `npm run check:duplication`\n- **Lines:** 9540–9690 (clone list), 9685 summary, 9688 `Found 1345 clones.`, 9690 `Code duplication check passed`\n- **Classification:** REAL-WARNING-TO-FIX\n\n```\n│ javascript │ 599 │ 138069 │ 1238246 │ 1345 │ 14625 (10.59%) │ 131359 (10.61%) │\nFound 1345 clones.\nCode duplication check passed\n```\n\n**Are they enforced or just printed? — Enforced.** `.jscpd.json` sets `\"threshold\": 11`, and jscpd exits non-zero above threshold; the step is a bare `npm run check:duplication` with no `|| true`. So this is a real gate — but it is 0.39 percentage points from tripping, and 1,345 clones are printed on every lint run regardless. Any moderately duplicative PR will turn this into a red build with a 150-line clone dump as the only diagnostic. The dominant offenders in the list are `tests/test-telegram-message-edit-error-handling.mjs` (12 clone pairs), `tests/test-pre-pr-failure-notifier-*.mjs` (7), `tests/test-issue-*-gitkeep-ignored.mjs` (7) — i.e. test boilerplate, which `.jscpd.json` does **not** ignore.\n\n---\n\n## SEVERITY 2 — Real warnings worth fixing\n\n### 2.1 `##[warning]File has N lines (approaching limit of 1500)` — 19 files at the edge\n- **Job/step:** `check-file-line-limits` / `bash scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh`\n- **Lines:** 14810, 14824, 14837, 14859, 14867, 14872, 14893, 14896, 14934, 14962, … (success log); 14638–15748 (failure log)\n- **Occurrences:** 20 in success log (18 of the \"extracting code\" variant + 1 \"inline scripts\" variant + 1 unrelated Node 20 warning); 20 in failure log\n- **Classification:** REAL-WARNING-TO-FIX\n\n```\n##[warning]File has 1500 lines (approaching limit of 1500). Consider extracting code to keep under 1350 lines to prevent concurrent PR merge issues (see issue #1141).\n##[warning]File has 1491 lines (approaching limit of 1500). Consider moving inline scripts to ./scripts/ folder.\n```\n\n**Root cause:** `scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh` warns in the 1350–1500 band and errors above 1500. **Two files are sitting at exactly 1500** — one line from a hard failure. This is a real, imminent build-breaker, not noise. The last warning is about `.github/workflows/release.yml` itself (1,491 lines).\n\n### 2.2 Node.js 20 deprecated action\n- **Job/step:** `Helm Release` / final annotation\n- **Line:** 49914 (last line of the success log)\n- **Occurrences:** 1\n- **Classification:** REAL-WARNING-TO-FIX (low urgency — currently auto-forced to Node 24)\n\n```\n##[warning]Node.js 20 is deprecated. The following actions target Node.js 20 but are being forced to run on Node.js 24: softprops/action-gh-release@v2. For more information see: https://github.blog/changelog/…-deprecation-of-node-20-on-github-actions-runners/\n```\n\n**Root cause:** the workflow sets `FORCE_JAVASCRIPT_ACTIONS_TO_NODE24: true` globally (visible in every job's env block), which papers over it. `softprops/action-gh-release@v2` is the only remaining node20 action; all others (`actions/checkout@v5`, `actions/setup-node@v5`, `actions/download-artifact@v8`, `docker/build-push-action@v7`) are already node24. Bump when upstream ships a node24 release.\n\n### 2.3 `npm warn allow-scripts` — @sentry/node-cpu-profiler postinstall blocked\n- **Job/step:** 7 sites — `lint`/`npm-install-with-retry.mjs ci` (4250), `test-execution`/`install` (16293), `test-execution`/`test-global-commands.sh` (18252), `memory-check-linux`/`install` (20497), `test-suites`/`install` (20944), `Release`/`install` (35329), `Release`/`version-and-commit.mjs` (35405)\n- **Occurrences:** 7 blocks × 4 lines = 28 lines (success); 20 lines (failure log)\n- **Classification:** REAL-WARNING-TO-FIX (currently harmless, silently degrading)\n\n```\nnpm warn allow-scripts 1 package has install scripts not yet covered by allowScripts:\nnpm warn allow-scripts   @sentry/node-cpu-profiler@2.4.2 (install: node scripts/check-build.js)\nnpm warn allow-scripts\nnpm warn allow-scripts Run `npm approve-scripts --allow-scripts-pending` to review, or `npm approve-scripts <pkg>` to allow.\n```\n\n**Root cause:** npm 11's new `allowScripts` gate. `package.json` has no `allowScripts` field, so `@sentry/node-cpu-profiler`'s `check-build.js` postinstall never runs — meaning the **native CPU profiler binary is never validated/built**. Sentry profiling silently falls back or no-ops. Either add an explicit `allowScripts` entry (documenting the decision) or drop the profiler dependency if profiling isn't used.\n\n### 2.4 `warn: incorrect peer dependency \"solid-js@1.9.14\"`\n- **Job/step:** all 4 Docker build jobs / `docker/build-push-action@v7`, layer `#13` (the `bun install -g` block)\n- **Lines:** 39093 (DinD amd64), 41217 (amd64), 43383 (arm64), 45584 (DinD arm64)\n- **Occurrences:** 4 (once per platform/image build)\n- **Classification:** BENIGN-NOISE (upstream), not actionable locally\n\n**Root cause (confirmed in `Dockerfile:139-140` / `Dockerfile.dind:148-149`):** emitted while resolving `bun install -g @link-assistant/agent` (the warning appears immediately before `installed @link-assistant/agent@0.25.0`, which pulls 481 packages). `solid-js` is a transitive peer of that package's Ink/OpenTUI-style rendering stack; the resolved version doesn't satisfy some dependent's peer range. Nothing in this repo pins it. Fix belongs upstream in `@link-assistant/agent`; locally it can only be silenced.\n\n### 2.5 `npm warn using --force Recommended protections disabled.`\n- **Job/step:** all 4 Docker build jobs / `docker/build-push-action@v7`, layer `#14`\n- **Lines:** 39159, 41283, 43449, 45650\n- **Occurrences:** 4\n- **Classification:** REAL-WARNING-TO-FIX (minor)\n\n**Root cause (`Dockerfile:152`, `Dockerfile.dind:157`):**\n```\nRUN npm install -g @playwright/mcp@latest --no-fund --force\n```\n`--force` disables npm's integrity/conflict protections for a single global install. The very next layer (`#15`) does verify the result (`playwright --version && npx --no-install @playwright/mcp --help | grep -q -- '--headless'`), so the blast radius is contained — but `--force` here is almost certainly vestigial (working around an old peer conflict). Try removing it; if the install still succeeds, delete the flag.\n\n---\n\n## SEVERITY 3 — Benign noise that should be silenced\n\n### 3.1 `DEP0040` punycode deprecation\n- **Job/step:** 14 sites across 8 jobs — mostly `actions/setup-node@v5` post-job cleanup, plus `jscpd`, `docs-validation.mjs`, `check-mjs-syntax.sh`, `run-tests.mjs`, `test-auto-fork-option.sh`, `upload-sourcemaps.mjs`\n- **Lines:** 4220, 9690, 11783, 11877, 12094, 12723, 16263, 20250, 20467, 20683, 20914, 33227, 35296, 37624 (success); 11 occurrences in failure log\n- **Occurrences:** 14 (+14 paired `(Use \\`node --trace-deprecation ...\\`)` lines)\n- **Classification:** BENIGN-NOISE\n\n```\n(node:2305) [DEP0040] DeprecationWarning: The `punycode` module is deprecated. Please use a userland alternative instead.\n(Use `node --trace-deprecation ...` to show where the warning was created)\n```\n\n**Root cause:** Node 24 deprecated the built-in `punycode`. A transitive dependency (typically `whatwg-url` → `tr46`, reached via older `request`/`node-fetch`-family packages) still requires it. Not fixable directly; resolves itself as the dep tree updates. Suppress with `NODE_OPTIONS=--no-deprecation` on the affected steps if the noise matters.\n\n### 3.2 `DEP0005` Buffer() deprecation\n- **Job/step:** `Docker Publish (Merge)` and `Docker Publish DinD (Merge)` / `actions/download-artifact@v8`\n- **Lines:** 46419, 47063\n- **Occurrences:** 2\n- **Classification:** BENIGN-NOISE\n\n```\n(node:2147) [DEP0005] DeprecationWarning: Buffer() is deprecated due to security and usability issues. Please use the Buffer.alloc(), Buffer.allocUnsafe(), or Buffer.from() methods instead.\n```\n\n**Root cause:** inside GitHub's own bundled `actions/download-artifact@v8` toolkit code, not this repo. Nothing to fix locally.\n\n### 3.3 git `init.defaultBranch` advice (7-line hint block)\n- **Job/step:** every job's `actions/checkout@v5` → `git init`\n- **Lines:** 79, 2223, 9786, 11973, 12818, 16128, 20346, 20779, 33306, 37712, 39936, 42045, 44220, 47713 (block start)\n- **Occurrences:** 14 blocks × 7 lines = 98 lines (success); 8 blocks in failure log\n- **Classification:** BENIGN-NOISE\n\n```\nhint: Using 'master' as the name for the initial branch. This default branch name\nhint: will change to \"main\" in Git 3.0. To configure the initial branch name\nhint: to use in all of your new repositories, which will suppress this warning,\nhint: call:\nhint: \tgit config --global init.defaultBranch <name>\nhint: Names commonly chosen instead of 'master' are 'main', 'trunk' and 'development'.\nhint: Disable this message with \"git config set advice.defaultBranchName false\"\n```\n\n**Root cause:** `actions/checkout` runs `git init` in a fresh workdir on a runner with no `init.defaultBranch` set (git 2.54.0). The branch name is irrelevant — checkout immediately fetches and checks out the real ref. Purely cosmetic; ~98 lines of the log.\n\n### 3.4 git `addIgnoredFile` advice\n- **Job/step:** `test-suites` / `run-tests.mjs`\n- **Lines:** 26702, 26707, 26713, 26720, 26727, 26739, … (7 blocks)\n- **Occurrences:** 7\n- **Classification:** GREP-FALSE-POSITIVE — this is asserted test output\n\n```\nThe following paths are ignored by one of your .gitignore files:\n.gitkeep\nhint: Use -f if you really want to add them.\n```\n\nImmediately followed by `✔ plain git add .gitkeep fails when the repo gitignores it (reproduces the bug)`. This is `tests/test-issue-1868-gitkeep-ignored.mjs` deliberately reproducing a bug. Leave alone.\n\n### 3.5 Retry chatter in test fixtures\n- **Job/step:** `test-suites` / `run-tests.mjs`\n- **Lines:** 24668–24696 (`Network error (attempt N/3)`, 11×), 29339–29361 (`[npm-install-with-retry] attempt N/M failed`, 6×), 30106–30114 (`[preinstall-use-m] attempt N/M failed`, 4×), 31361–31443 (`Bot launch attempt N failed (409): Conflict`, 8×)\n- **Classification:** GREP-FALSE-POSITIVE\n\nAll four families are **unit tests exercising retry logic against mocks**, not real failures. Confirmed by surrounding assertions (`✅ non-retryable: \"SyntaxError: Unexpected token\"`, `✅ detects npm error codes regardless of case`, `ℹ️ command-stream-v-latest already present …; treating as success despite npm error`). Every enclosing suite reports `0 failed`. Same for the 5× `ℹ️ Error issue creation is disabled by CLI configuration.` and the `--sentry` / `--disable-report-issue` lines, which are just `--help` output captured by the `test-execution` job.\n\n---\n\n## Failure-hiding constructs (`|| true` / `continue-on-error` / `set +e`)\n\nI audited the whole workflow and the shell scripts. **There are no `continue-on-error:` keys and no `set +e` anywhere** in `.github/workflows/` or `scripts/`; all 9 shell scripts start with `set -e`. Six `|| true`-class sites exist:\n\n| Line (release.yml) | Construct | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| 320 | `timeout 10s ./src/solve.mjs --version \\|\\| true` | BENIGN — smoke test only; the preceding `--help` on line 318 does the real work and its output is verified at log line 17145 |\n| 330 | `timeout 10s ./src/hive.mjs --version \\|\\| true` | BENIGN — same pattern |\n| 359 | `timeout 30s ./src/hive.mjs … --dry-run … \\| tee hive_dry_run.log \\|\\| true` | **WEAK** — see below |\n| 369 | `timeout 10s ./src/solve.mjs … --dry-run … \\| head -20 \\|\\| true` | **WEAK** — see below |\n| 558 | `grep -E 'unbound variable' build-output.log … \\|\\| true` | BENIGN — inside an `if` that already matched; this is just the re-print before `exit 1` |\n| 1466 | `npx prettier --write \".changeset/*.md\" \\|\\| true` | BENIGN — cosmetic formatting in the manual-changeset dispatch path |\n\n**Lines 359 and 369 are the two genuinely weak spots.** Line 359's assertion is self-defeating:\n\n```bash\ntimeout 30s ./src/hive.mjs … --dry-run … | tee hive_dry_run.log || true\nif grep -q \"solve.*--dry-run.*--skip-claude-check\" hive_dry_run.log; then\n  echo \"hive correctly passes --dry-run and --skip-claude-check flags to solve command\"\nelse\n  echo \"Could not verify flag propagation in dry-run mode (may be due to no issues found)\"\nfi\n```\n\nBoth branches print and both exit 0 — so if `hive.mjs` crashes outright, or stops propagating flags to `solve`, the step still passes with a reassuring message. Line 369 is worse: it discards the exit code *and* pipes through `head -20`, so the step asserts nothing at all beyond \"the binary was executable\". These are the only two places in the workflow where a real regression could pass unnoticed. Note that in this run the `else` branch did **not** fire — flag propagation was verified — so nothing is currently broken there.\n\n---\n\n## What the failure log confirms\n\n`run-29125268021-failure.log` is a useful control. Its single `##[error]` is at line 26769:\n\n```\nFAIL: /codex invalid --think reports each choice once after URL probing\n  Missing expected rejection.\nTotal: 4, Passed: 3, Failed: 1\nFailed test files:\n  - tests/test-telegram-options-before-url.mjs (exit 1)\n##[error]Process completed with exit code 1.\n```\n\nJob `test-suites`, step `node scripts/run-tests.mjs`. This is the important negative result: **a single failing assertion in one of 318 test files does correctly propagate to a red build.** The test harness's exit-code plumbing is sound, which is what lets me classify all the `0 failed` lines in the success log as trustworthy rather than merely unreported. The failure log also carries the same benign families (20 allow-scripts lines, 11 DEP0040, 8 git-init hint blocks, 20 line-limit warnings) — and notably it shows the line-limit pressure was already at `1500/1500` back on 2026-07-10, i.e. this has been sitting one line from the cliff for over a week.\n\n---\n\n## Recommended order of work\n\n1. **Fix the publish verification loop** (`scripts/publish-to-npm.mjs`) — poll with backoff, treat `EPUBLISHCONFLICT` as success. This is the only finding that can produce a genuinely broken release.\n2. **Split the two 1500/1500-line files** — an imminent hard build break, already stale for a week.\n3. **`npm pkg fix`** the `bin` paths in `package.json` — affects the published artifact and is normally invisible.\n4. **Trim the sourcemap step** — drop `./tests`, and either remove the step or silence its warning class; recovers ~1,200 log lines.\n5. Decide on `allowScripts` for `@sentry/node-cpu-profiler` (or drop the dep).\n6. Strengthen release.yml lines 359/369 so the dry-run smoke tests can actually fail.\n7. Cosmetic: set `init.defaultBranch` / `advice.defaultBranchName=false` (−98 lines), `NODE_OPTIONS=--no-deprecation` on noisy steps, drop `--force` from the Dockerfile playwright install, add `tests/**` to `.jscpd.json` ignores or raise headroom above 10.61%."
