[2026-07-19T12:36:30.649Z] [INFO]         "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n## 1. Primary Request and Intent\n\nA single user turn set the whole task. The user is an AI issue solver operating on:\n- **Repo/working dir:** `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784463865325` (link-assistant/hive-mind)\n- **Branch (push ONLY to this):** `issue-2082-90c17c1e7d2a`\n- **Issue:** https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2082 — *\"Check for all false positives, false negatives, warnings and errors in CI/CD and fix them all\"*\n- **PR (already exists — update, do NOT create new):** https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/2083\n\nExplicit deliverables from the user message:\n1. \"Download all logs and collect data related about the issue to this repository, and compile that data into the `./dev/log/issues/2082/pulls/2083` folder.\"\n2. \"Use the collected evidence to do a deep analysis (search online for additional facts and data), reconstruct the timeline/sequence of events, list each and every requirement from the issue, find the root cause of each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement. Also check online for known existing components/libraries that solve a similar problem or can help.\"\n3. \"If there is not enough data to find the actual root cause, add debug output and a verbose mode (if not already present) so the root cause can be found on the next iteration. Keep the default state switched off.\"\n4. \"If the issue is related to another repository/project, report issues on GitHub for that project when possible. Each report must contain reproducible examples, workarounds, and suggestions for fixing the issue in code.\"\n5. \"Double-check that the requirements are fully applied to the entire codebase: if an issue exists in multiple places, apply it in all of them.\"\n\nRequirements derived from issue #2082 body itself:\n- **R1** Find & fix all CI/CD **false positives** (green checks that verify nothing)\n- **R2** Find & fix all CI/CD **false negatives** (real failures reported as success)\n- **R3** Find & fix all CI/CD **warnings**\n- **R4** Find & fix all CI/CD **errors**\n- **R5** Compare the **full file tree** against `https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template` and reuse all best practices\n- **R6** \"if the same issue is found in template report issue also in templates\" → file upstream issues\n- **R7** Follow `docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md`\n- **R8** \"plan and execute everything in this single pull request … until it is each and every requirement fully addressed\"\n\nStanding operational constraints from the user message: commit atomic steps to the branch; create reproducing tests BEFORE fixes; keep debug/experiment scripts in `./experiments` and real-world use cases in `./examples`; save large command output to files; run local CI checks (lint etc.) before pushing; download CI logs to `ci-logs/` and Read them; use `gh pr edit` to update PR 2083 and `gh pr ready 2083` when finished; verify clean `git status` at the end; merge default branch into the PR branch; check all three GitHub comment API endpoints (`/pulls/N/comments`, `/issues/N/comments`, `/pulls/N/reviews`) with `--paginate`.\n\n## 2. Key Technical Concepts\n\n- **GitHub Actions**: `timeout-minutes`, `concurrency`/`cancel-in-progress`, `always()` vs `!cancelled()`, job `permissions`, `continue-on-error`, action version pinning, `FORCE_JAVASCRIPT_ACTIONS_TO_NODE24`\n- **`command-stream`'s `\n\n**: fail-soft semantics — resolves with `.code` instead of throwing. Core root-cause mechanism.\n- **`set -euo pipefail`** (bash fail-fast) vs the `.mjs` rewrite that lost it\n- **Changesets** release automation (`changeset publish`, `changeset:version`)\n- **npm registry read-after-write propagation lag** → E404 on immediate verification\n- **Helm chart publishing** via a `gh-pages` branch + `helm repo index`\n- **Sentry sourcemap upload** (`@sentry/cli sourcemaps upload`) on a project with no build/transpile step\n- **jscpd** duplication threshold gating; **secretlint**; **lychee** link checking\n- **npm 11 `allowScripts`** postinstall gating\n- `use-m` dynamic package loading, `lino-arguments` config\n\n## 3. Files and Code Sections\n\n### `scripts/helm-release.mjs` (137 lines) — THE critical finding\nEvery git command is a bare `await $\\`...\\``, and `\n\n never throws, so the wrapping `try/catch` (lines 59–137) is decorative.\n```js\n  // Checkout gh-pages branch\n  console.log('Checking out gh-pages branch...');\n  await \n\ngit fetch origin gh-pages:gh-pages`;\n  await \n\ngit checkout gh-pages`;          // line 105 — FAILS, swallowed\n\n  // Update Helm repository index\n  await \n\ncp .helm-packages/*.tgz .`;      // line 110\n  await \n\nhelm repo index . --url \"${helmRepoUrl}\"`;  // line 111\n  ...\n  await \n\ngit add -f *.tgz index.yaml`;    // line 118\n  const commitResult = await \n\ngit commit -m \"Release Helm chart version ${version}\"`.run({ capture: true });\n  if (commitResult.code !== 0) { console.log('No changes to commit'); }\n  await \n\ngit push origin gh-pages`;       // line 125 — \"Everything up-to-date\"\n  await \n\ngit checkout -`;                 // line 130 — FAILS, swallowed\n  console.log(`Helm chart version ${version} released successfully!`);  // line 133\n```\nCalled from **two** jobs: `.github/workflows/release.yml:1042` (`helm-release`) and `:1432` (`helm-release-instant`).\n\n### `experiments/issue-2082-command-stream-throw.mjs` — CREATED (proof)\n```js\n#!/usr/bin/env node\n// Experiment for issue #2082: does command-stream's `\n\n throw on a non-zero exit code?\nimport { ensureUseM } from '../src/use-m-bootstrap.lib.mjs';\nconst use = await ensureUseM();\nconst { $ } = await use('command-stream');\nlet threw = false; let result;\ntry { result = await \n\ngit checkout definitely-not-a-branch-2082`; }\ncatch (e) { threw = true; console.log('THREW:', e.message); }\nconsole.log('threw          =', threw);\nconsole.log('result.code    =', result?.code);\nconsole.log('VERDICT:', threw ? 'throws -> try/catch works' : 'DOES NOT THROW -> failures are silently ignored');\n```\nOutput: `threw = false`, `result.code = 1`, `VERDICT: DOES NOT THROW -> failures are silently ignored`\n\n### `scripts/version-and-commit.mjs:205–232` — same defect class\n```js\n      await \n\ngit add -A`;\n      const escapedMessage = commitMessage.replace(/\"/g, '\\\\\"');\n      await \n\ngit commit -m \"${escapedMessage}\"`;\n      // Push directly to main\n      await \n\ngit push origin main`;                 // line 219 — unchecked\n      console.log('Version bump committed and pushed to main');\n      setOutput('version_committed', 'true');\n```\n\n### `scripts/publish-to-npm.mjs:145–181` — publish race\n```js\nexport async function publishWithRetry({ runner, version, maxRetries = DEFAULT_MAX_RETRIES, ... }) {\n  for (let attempt = 1; attempt <= maxRetries; attempt++) {\n    logger.log(`Publish attempt ${attempt} of ${maxRetries}...`);\n    const result = await runner('npm', ['run', 'changeset:publish']);   // re-runs FULL publish on retry\n    const analysis = analyzePublishResult(result);\n    if (analysis.ok) {\n      logger.log(`Publish command reported success; verifying ${PACKAGE_NAME}@${version} on npm...`);\n      const published = await isVersionPublished(runner, version);      // immediate, no backoff\n      if (published) { return { ok: true, attempt }; }\n      lastReason = 'post-publish verification failed: version not found on npm';\n```\n\n### `scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh` — landmine\n`LIMIT=1500`, `WARN_THRESHOLD=1350`, fails only when `-gt 1500`. **Four files sit at exactly 1500**: `src/telegram-solve-queue.lib.mjs`, `src/solve.mjs`, `src/codex.lib.mjs`, `src/claude.lib.mjs`. `src/hive.mjs`=1498, `.github/workflows/release.yml`=1491.\n\n### `scripts/check-mjs-syntax.sh` — coverage gap\nLoops `*.mjs`, `src/*.mjs`, `tests/*.mjs`. **`scripts/` is never syntax-checked** (ironically including the broken `helm-release.mjs`), and the `tests/` loop lacks the `timeout 10s` the other two loops have. Mitigated: `package.json:24` lint DOES cover `'scripts/**/*.{js,mjs,cjs}'`.\n\n### `scripts/test-auto-fork-option.sh` / `test-global-commands.sh` / `verify-log-file-contents.sh` — vacuous\n```bash\ntimeout 10s ./src/solve.mjs ... --auto-fork --dry-run 2>&1 | tee solve_auto_fork.log || true\nif grep -qE \"(auto-fork|Auto-fork)\" solve_auto_fork.log; then\n  echo \"solve.mjs recognizes --auto-fork flag\"\nelse\n  echo \"Could not verify --auto-fork flag in solve output\"   # <-- no exit 1\nfi\n```\n```bash\ntimeout 10s hive --version || true\ntimeout 10s hive --help || echo \"Help command completed\"\necho \"'hive' global command works\"      # <-- unconditional\n```\n`test-global-commands.sh:34,56` (`npm unlink -g ... || true`) are legitimate trap cleanup — leave alone.\n\n### `.github/workflows/release.yml:45–52` — concurrency divergence\n```yaml\nconcurrency:\n  group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}\n  cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' }}\nenv:\n  FORCE_JAVASCRIPT_ACTIONS_TO_NODE24: true\n```\nTemplate has `!= 'refs/heads/main'` plus `group: main-writer-${{ github.repository }}-main` / `cancel-in-progress: false` on `release` and `instant-release`. Also template sets `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/KEY_0/VALUE_0 = init.defaultBranch=main` which hive-mind lacks.\n\n### Analysis docs CREATED under `dev/log/issues/2082/pulls/2083/analysis/`\n- `F1-helm-release-false-negative.md` — full root cause, 9-step failure chain, timeline, proposed fix\n- `F2-template-gap-analysis.md` — 19-row gap table + prioritized plan + \"hive-mind is ahead\" note\n- `F3-vacuous-tests-false-positives.md` — vacuous test scripts\n\n### Evidence artifacts saved\n`github/` (issue-2082.json/.txt, issue-comments.json, pr-2083.json, pr-comments.json, pr-review-comments.json, pr-reviews.json, runs-recent.json — all comment files are empty `[]`), `ci-logs/` (run-29647956700-success.log 49,914 lines; run-29125268021-failure.log 31,365 lines; run-29686761617.json), `templates/` (template-release.yml, template-links.yml, template-BEST-PRACTICES.md, ci-timeouts.test.js, workflow-reliability.test.js, push-main-with-rebase-retry.sh, smoke-test-package.mjs, template-jscpd.json, template-secretlintrc.json, template-file-tree.txt), `analysis/` (published-index.yaml, command-stream-throw-experiment.log, helm-release-failure-excerpt.log, helm-release-git-history.log, npm-publish-race-excerpt.log, files-near-line-limit.txt, hive-mind-file-tree.txt, repo-head.txt)\n\n## 4. Errors and fixes\n\n- **`jq: command not found` (exit 127)** — jq is unavailable in this environment. Worked around using `tr`/`grep`/`gh --json` field selection instead. Must avoid `jq` going forward.\n- **Shell cwd reset** — one Bash call reported \"Shell cwd was reset to /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784463865325\". Used explicit `cd` prefixes afterwards.\n- No user corrections or feedback were received (only one user turn so far).\n\n## 5. Problem Solving\n\n**Solved / fully root-caused:**\n\n**F1 (CRITICAL, false negative) — Helm release publishes nothing while reporting success.**\nProven failure chain: (1) `gh-pages` was created from main's tree so it also contains `helm/hive-mind/Chart.yaml`; (2) `helm-release.mjs:68-71` modifies that file; (3) `git checkout gh-pages` aborts (\"local changes would be overwritten\"); (4) `\n\n swallows it; (5) execution continues on `main`; (6) commit lands on main (`[main f723e208]`); (7) `git push origin gh-pages` → \"Everything up-to-date\"; (8) `git checkout -` fails; (9) prints \"released successfully!\", exit 0, job green.\nProduction proof: published `index.yaml` newest entry is **0.38.8, created 2025-12-11**; gh-pages tip `dd31d941` is \"Release Helm chart version 0.38.8\"; package.json is at **2.8.3**. ~7 months of silent no-op releases.\nRegression origin: commit `5b7e60d7` (2025-12-23) \"refactor: convert CI/CD shell scripts to .mjs format\" replaced `helm-release.sh` (which opened with `set -euo pipefail`) with the `.mjs` version.\n\n**F2 — 19 template gaps** incl. 4 `timeout-minutes` for ~26 jobs, no `ci-timeouts.test.js`, concurrency divergence, no secretlint config/step despite the dep being installed and documented, jscpd threshold 11 vs 0, `always()` in 10 jobs, missing `links.yml`, `@v5` vs `@v6` actions, no `smoke-test-package.mjs`.\n\n**F3 — vacuous test scripts** that can never fail.\n\n**F4 (from log agent, verified) — npm publish double-publish race**: attempt 1 succeeds and creates tag `v2.8.3`, immediate `npm view` returns E404 (registry replica lag ~6s), verifier declares failure, attempt 2 re-runs full `changeset publish` and legitimately errors \"You cannot publish over the previously published versions\", attempt 3 succeeds. Green only by luck of the 3-attempt budget.\n\n**F5 — four files at exactly 1500/1500 lines** — one added line breaks CI.\n\n**F6 — 593 Sentry sourcemap warnings**: project has no build step (`build:pre` is only `chmod +x`), so no `.map` files exist; the step also uploads 357 test files.\n\n**Important negative/control result:** the failure log (run 29125268021) proves test exit codes DO propagate correctly (a single failing assertion produced `##[error]Process completed with exit code 1`), which validates trusting the `0 failed` lines in the success log.\n\n**Nothing has been committed, pushed, or code-fixed yet.**\n\n## 6. All user messages\n\nThere has been exactly **one** user message — the initial task prompt. Verbatim key constraints:\n\n- \"Download all logs and collect data related about the issue to this repository, and compile that data into the ./dev/log/issues/2082/pulls/2083 folder.\"\n- \"Use the collected evidence to do a deep analysis (search online for additional facts and data), reconstruct the timeline/sequence of events, list each and every requirement from the issue, find the root cause of each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement. Also check online for known existing components/libraries that solve a similar problem or can help.\"\n- \"If there is not enough data to find the actual root cause, add debug output and a verbose mode (if not already present) so the root cause can be found on the next iteration. Keep the default state switched off.\"\n- \"If the issue is related to another repository/project, report issues on GitHub for that project when possible. Each report must contain reproducible examples, workarounds, and suggestions for fixing the issue in code.\"\n- \"Double-check that the requirements are fully applied to the entire codebase: if an issue exists in multiple places, apply it in all of them.\"\n- \"Proceed.\"\n\n(Subsequent messages in the transcript were automated background-task notifications from subagents, explicitly flagged as NOT user input and NOT approval.)\n\n## 7. Pending Tasks\n\n1. Write the **master README.md** in `dev/log/issues/2082/pulls/2083/` — requirements list (R1–R8), consolidated timeline, all findings F1–F6+, root causes, solution plans. (Was in progress when summarization was requested.)\n2. Record remaining findings as analysis docs (F4 publish race, F5 line limits, F6 sourcemaps, warning inventory).\n3. **Search online** for existing libraries/components solving these problems (explicit user request, NOT yet done) — e.g. helm chart publishing actions (`helm/chart-releaser-action`), `stefanzweifel/git-auto-commit-action`, zx vs command-stream, npm publish verification tooling.\n4. Implement fixes: helm-release exit-code checking + worktree-based publishing + post-publish verification; `version-and-commit.mjs` push retry; `timeout-minutes` on all jobs + port `ci-timeouts.test.js`; de-vacuum the `|| true` test scripts; `check-mjs-syntax.sh` coverage; secretlint wiring; `always()`→`!cancelled()`; `GIT_CONFIG_*` env; publish-verification backoff; split the four 1500-line files; sourcemap step trim; `npm pkg fix` for bin paths.\n5. Write reproducing tests BEFORE fixes (user requirement).\n6. **File upstream issue(s)** on `link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template` — the template lacks hive-mind's `detectPublishFailure()`/`FAILURE_PATTERNS` hardening (R6).\n7. Add a changeset / version bump for release.\n8. Commit atomically, push to `issue-2082-90c17c1e7d2a`, update PR 2083 via `gh pr edit`, merge main in, verify CI, `gh pr ready 2083`.\n\n## 8. Current Work\n\nImmediately before the summary request I was **verifying the second agent's two most consequential claims first-hand** before folding them into the master report, having just written F1/F2/F3.\n\nI had confirmed:\n- The npm publish race verbatim from the log (saved to `analysis/npm-publish-race-excerpt.log`), showing `Publish attempt 1 of 3` → `🦋 success packages published successfully: @link-assistant/hive-mind@2.8.3` → `🦋 Creating git tag... New tag: v2.8.3` → `Publish command reported success; verifying ...` → `npm error code E404 / npm error 404 No match found for version 2.8.3`.\n- The line-limit landmine, finding it **worse** than the agent reported — **four** files at exactly 1500 (agent said two), saved to `analysis/files-near-line-limit.txt`.\n\nMy very last action was reading `scripts/publish-to-npm.mjs:140–181` to pin the exact root cause of the publish race: `publishWithRetry` calls `isVersionPublished` immediately with no backoff, and on a false-negative verification it re-invokes the **entire** `npm run changeset:publish` rather than merely re-polling the registry.\n\nMy message to the user at that point was: *\"Both confirmed — and the line-limit issue is worse than reported: four files sit at exactly 1500/1500. Let me compile the master report.\"*\n\n## 9. Optional Next Step\n\nWrite `dev/log/issues/2082/pulls/2083/README.md` — the master analysis document consolidating requirements R1–R8, the reconstructed timeline, findings F1–F6 with root causes, and per-requirement solution plans — then continue with the still-unstarted explicit user request to \"check online for known existing components/libraries that solve a similar problem or can help\" (e.g. `helm/chart-releaser-action` for F1).\n\nThis is directly in line with my last stated intent — \"Let me compile the master report\" — and with the user's explicit instruction to \"compile that data into the ./dev/log/issues/2082/pulls/2083 folder … reconstruct the timeline/sequence of events, list each and every requirement from the issue, find the root cause of each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/box/.claude/projects/-tmp-gh-issue-solver-1784463865325/f5664df3-3134-4624-b8f7-5ed40a35b7d2.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."
