[2026-07-19T12:36:51.607Z] [INFO]           "description": "Research existing CI/CD libraries",
[2026-07-19T12:36:51.607Z] [INFO]           "prompt": "Research online (WebSearch + WebFetch) for existing, well-known components/libraries/GitHub Actions that solve these specific problems. For each, report: name, URL, what it solves, maturity/popularity, and whether it's a good fit for a Node.js repo that publishes to npm + Docker + Helm via GitHub Actions and Changesets.\n\nProblems to research:\n1. **Publishing a Helm chart repository from CI to a gh-pages branch.** Currently a hand-rolled `helm repo index` + `git checkout gh-pages` + commit + push script that silently no-ops. Look specifically at `helm/chart-releaser-action` and `helm/chart-releaser`, plus alternatives (e.g. OCI registry publishing to GHCR via `helm push`, `stefanzweifel/git-auto-commit-action`, `peaceiris/actions-gh-pages`). Which is the current best practice in 2026 — gh-pages index or OCI/GHCR?\n\n2. **Shell-command execution in Node scripts with fail-fast semantics** — the root cause here is `command-stream`'s `$` resolving instead of throwing on non-zero exit. Compare `google/zx`, `execa`, `dax-sh`, and Node's own `node:child_process`. Which throw by default on non-zero exit? Report exact default behavior of each with a citation.\n\n3. **Verifying an npm publish actually landed** (registry read-after-write propagation lag causing E404 immediately after a successful publish). Is this a known documented npm registry behavior? Find authoritative sources (npm docs, GitHub issues, npm status/incident writeups) about replication lag on `npm view` after `npm publish`. Are there existing retry/verify utilities or recommended patterns?\n\n4. **Pushing to a protected/busy main branch from CI with rebase-retry** — existing actions/libraries (e.g. `ad-m/github-push-action`, `stefanzweifel/git-auto-commit-action`) and whether any handle non-fast-forward retry.\n\n5. **Enforcing `timeout-minutes` on every GitHub Actions job** — existing linters (`rhysd/actionlint`, `zizmorcore/zizmor`, OpenSSF Scorecard) that can catch missing timeouts, missing `permissions`, unpinned actions. Does actionlint or zizmor check for missing timeout-minutes specifically? Be precise — do not guess.\n\n6. **Sentry sourcemap upload for a project with NO build step** — is uploading sourcemaps meaningful when source is shipped unbundled/untranspiled? What does Sentry's own documentation recommend for plain ESM Node projects?\n\nBe rigorous: cite URLs, quote the relevant doc text, and clearly separate what you verified from what you inferred. Do not fabricate. If you can't verify something, say so.\n\nReturn a markdown report suitable for saving directly to a file.",
