[2026-07-19T12:37:04.149Z] [INFO]         "content": "Web search results for query: \"actionlint zizmor missing timeout-minutes check rule\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Feature: Require or recommend the timeout-minutes property for all jobs #1023 by EmmanuelBerkowicz · Pull Request #1067 · zizmorcore/zizmor\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/zizmorcore/zizmor/pull/1067\"},{\"title\":\"Feature Request: add rule to force `timeout-minutes` · Issue #49 · rhysd/actionlint\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/issues/49\"},{\"title\":\"[BUG]: `timeout-minutes: 0.5` causes deserialization failure · Issue #1672 · zizmorcore/zizmor\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/zizmorcore/zizmor/issues/1672\"},{\"title\":\"Feature: Require or recommend the `timeout-minutes` property for all jobs · Issue #1023 · zizmorcore/zizmor\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/zizmorcore/zizmor/issues/1023\"},{\"title\":\"actionlint/docs/checks.md at v1.7.4 · rhysd/actionlint\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/blob/v1.7.4/docs/checks.md\"},{\"title\":\"Harden your GitHub Actions Workflows with zizmor, dependency pinning, and dependency cooldowns - Matthias Schoettle\",\"url\":\"https://mattsch.com/blog/2026/03/28/harden-your-github-actions-workflows-with-zizmor-dependency-pinning-and-dependency-cooldowns/\"},{\"title\":\"actionlint/docs/checks.md at v1.7.12 · rhysd/actionlint\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/blob/v1.7.12/docs/checks.md\"},{\"title\":\"actionlint/docs/checks.md at main · rhysd/actionlint\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/blob/main/docs/checks.md\"},{\"title\":\"actionlint/docs/checks.md at v1.7.11 · rhysd/actionlint\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/blob/v1.7.11/docs/checks.md\"},{\"title\":\"actionlint/docs/checks.md at v1.7.9 · rhysd/actionlint\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/blob/v1.7.9/docs/checks.md\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about actionlint, zizmor, and the missing timeout-minutes check rule:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe search results reveal an important distinction between two tools:\n\n1. **Actionlint** - Actionlint does not currently have functionality to disable each rules, and only the -ignore option can ignore errors. A feature request was made for actionlint to add a rule that warns about missing `timeout-minutes`, but this doesn't appear to be implemented in actionlint itself.\n\n2. **Zizmor** - Zizmor implements a new audit rule that detects missing timeout-minutes property on GitHub Actions jobs to prevent runaway jobs from consuming runner minutes. The feature was requested to enforce or recommend the use of a timeout-minutes property on all jobs as part of the \"pedantic\" or \"auditor\" persona.\n\n## Key Context\n\n- Jobs which call a reusable workflow (with uses) do not support timeout-minutes, as the property needs to be defined in the jobs within the reusable workflow that it calls\n- GitHub Actions accepts fractional minute values for timeout-minutes at both the job and step level\n\nSo if you're looking for a missing timeout-minutes check rule, you'll want to use **zizmor** rather than actionlint, as zizmor has implemented this audit rule specifically for this purpose.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."
