[2026-07-19T12:37:06.525Z] [INFO]         "content": "Web search results for query: \"helm chart-releaser-action vs OCI GHCR helm push best practice 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"How to Release Helm Charts with GitHub Actions\",\"url\":\"https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-01-27-release-helm-charts-github-actions/view\"},{\"title\":\"Helm OCI Push · Actions · GitHub Marketplace · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/marketplace/actions/helm-oci-push\"},{\"title\":\"Helm Chart Repo (ghcr.io) · Actions · GitHub Marketplace · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/marketplace/actions/helm-chart-repo-ghcr-io\"},{\"title\":\"Helm OCI Chart Releaser · Actions · GitHub Marketplace · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/marketplace/actions/helm-oci-chart-releaser\"},{\"title\":\"Publish helm charts also as an OCI package (e.g. on GHCR/ECR registry) · Issue #1070 · aws/eks-charts\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/aws/eks-charts/issues/1070\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - appany/helm-oci-chart-releaser: Push Helm Charts to OCI-based registries · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/appany/helm-oci-chart-releaser\"},{\"title\":\"Helm OCI Charts Releaser · Actions · GitHub Marketplace · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/marketplace/actions/helm-oci-charts-releaser\"},{\"title\":\"Helm Chart CI/CD with GitHub Actions\",\"url\":\"https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-01-17-helm-cicd-github-actions/view\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - JimCronqvist/action-helm-chart-repo: Turn your repo with charts into a Helm Chart Registry using GitHub Container Registry (OCI-based)\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/JimCronqvist/action-helm-chart-repo\"},{\"title\":\"ci-github-container/actions/helm/release-chart/README.md at main · hoverkraft-tech/ci-github-container\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/hoverkraft-tech/ci-github-container/blob/main/actions/helm/release-chart/README.md\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about helm chart-releaser-action vs OCI GHCR helm push best practices in 2026:\n\n## Key Differences\n\nThe chart-releaser-action by Helm uses GitHub Pages as the charts repo, while OCI-based alternatives like GHCR represent a shift in approach.\n\nHelm natively supports OCI-based registries since helm v3.8.0, making ghcr.io more practical than using GitHub Pages as a workaround.\n\n## Current Best Practice Approaches\n\nSeveral strategies have emerged in 2026:\n\n1. **Native OCI Approach**: Login to GHCR and use `helm push` to push charts directly to `oci://ghcr.io` registry.\n\n2. **Hybrid Strategy**: Run chart-releaser-action first, then push the packaged charts to GHCR using `helm push` with OCI paths.\n\n3. **Specialized Actions**: Chart-releaser-action outputs changed_charts that can be fed directly to OCI push actions like helm-oci-push-action.\n\n4. **Dedicated OCI Releasers**: Dedicated OCI chart releasers use Helm to login and push charts into an OCI registry, while using gh CLI to create and update repository releases.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nUsing OCI registries like GHCR works on private repos without paying for an Enterprise plan, making it an attractive alternative to the traditional chart-releaser-action approach. The trend in 2026 appears to favor direct OCI registry publishing over GitHub Pages-based approaches.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."
