[2026-07-19T12:37:33.516Z] [INFO]         "content": "# Does Execa Throw by Default on Non-Zero Exit Code?\n\nBased on the README provided, the documentation mentions \"Detailed errors\" as a feature and shows an `ExecaError` example, but the specific content about the `reject`/`throwOnError` option is not included in the visible text.\n\nHowever, the README does reference comprehensive error handling documentation: \"❌ [Errors](/sindresorhus/execa/blob/main/docs/errors.md)\" and demonstrates error handling with try/catch blocks, suggesting that execa does throw errors by default on command failure.\n\nTo get the precise details about the `reject` or `throwOnError` option behavior, you would need to consult the full [errors documentation](https://github.com/sindresorhus/execa/blob/main/docs/errors.md) linked in the README, as those specific option details aren't quoted in this excerpt."
