[2026-07-19T12:37:48.536Z] [INFO]         "content": "Web search results for query: \"dax-sh dsherret dax noThrow \"throws\" non-zero exit code default README\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"dax/README.md at main · dsherret/dax\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/dsherret/dax/blob/main/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - novusnota-forks/dsherret-dax: Cross-platform shell tools for Deno and Node.js inspired by zx. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/novusnota-forks/dsherret-dax\"},{\"title\":\"dax-sh - npm\",\"url\":\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/dax-sh?activeTab=readme\"},{\"title\":\"Throw exception on nonzero exit code · Issue #5347 · nushell/nushell\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nushell/nushell/issues/5347\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - dsherret/dax: Cross-platform shell tools for Deno and Node.js inspired by zx. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/dsherret/dax\"},{\"title\":\"Shell - Bun\",\"url\":\"https://bun.com/docs/runtime/shell\"},{\"title\":\"dax — cross-platform shell tools for Deno and Node.js\",\"url\":\"https://dax.land/\"},{\"title\":\"stack trace tranucated · Issue #150 · dsherret/dax\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/dsherret/dax/issues/150\"},{\"title\":\"dsherret/dax - GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://www.tkcnn.com/github/dsherret/dax.html\"},{\"title\":\"dsherret/dax\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/dsherret/dax/issues\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about dax's behavior regarding non-zero exit codes and the `noThrow()` method:\n\n## Default Behavior\n\nBy default, commands will throw an error on non-zero exit code. For example:\n\n```javascript\nawait $`exit 123`; // Uncaught Error: Exited with code: 123\n```\n\n## Using noThrow()\n\nTo disable this behaviour, you can run a command with `.noThrow()`, which returns the result object. You can also apply `.noThrow()` only for certain exit codes.\n\nExample:\n```javascript\nconst result = await $`exit 123`.noThrow();\nconsole.log(result.code); // 123\n```\n\n## Custom Default Behavior\n\nIf you want it to not throw by default, you can build a custom `$`. For instance, you can use the `CommandBuilder` API to set `.noThrow()` globally for all commands executed with that instance.\n\nThis information is documented in the official dax README on GitHub and the npm package documentation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."
