[2026-07-19T12:37:51.532Z] [INFO]         "content": "Web search results for query: \"npm publish then npm view E404 replication lag registry propagation delay\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"NPM Trusted Publishing: The “Weird” 404 Error and the Node.js 24 Fix | by Kenrick Tandrian | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@kenricktan11/npm-trusted-publishers-the-weird-404-error-and-the-node-js-24-fix-a9f1d717a5dd\"},{\"title\":\"How to Fix 'Package Not Publishing to npm' Error: Resolving 'Not in npm Registry' (E404 Not Found) — w3tutorials.net\",\"url\":\"https://www.w3tutorials.net/blog/package-is-not-publishing-to-npm-not-in-the-npm-registry/\"},{\"title\":\"npm publish 404 Not Found - PUT · Issue #1637 · npm/cli\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/npm/cli/issues/1637\"},{\"title\":\"Surviving the npm ERR! 404 with private packages | by Marco Rapaccini | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://rapaccinim.medium.com/surviving-the-npm-err-404-with-private-packages-b413d80fb860\"},{\"title\":\"can't publish to npm registry org, PUT 404 · Issue #11098 · pnpm/pnpm\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/pnpm/pnpm/issues/11098\"},{\"title\":\"Receive 404 error when trying to npm publish instead of 401 (#321249) · Issues · GitLab.org / GitLab · GitLab\",\"url\":\"https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/gitlab/-/issues/321249\"},{\"title\":\"npm publish gives E404 for private package · Issue #18932 · npm/npm\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/npm/npm/issues/18932\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the npm publish E404 error and registry propagation:\n\n## E404 Error After npm publish\n\nThe E404 error that occurs after publishing to npm typically relates to **registry synchronization and propagation delays**, though the search results reveal several nuanced causes:\n\n### Registry Propagation Lag\nWhen an OIDC handshake fails, the registry treats the user as an anonymous user, and anonymous users can't PUT (publish), resulting in the misleading 404 Not Found. This can occur when your npm CLI version doesn't support the latest protocols required by the registry.\n\n### Common Causes of E404 During publish\n\nAuthentication issues (expired/invalid auth tokens), version conflicts (attempting to republish an existing version), typos or case sensitivity in package names, cache corruption, and network/firewall blocking can all trigger E404 errors.\n\n### npm view E404 Issue\n\nTrusted Publishing requires npm CLI version 11.5.1 or later, with Node.js 22 shipping with npm v10 and Node.js 24 shipping with npm v11, and because Node 22 uses npm v10, the CLI doesn't support the latest OIDC handshake protocols required by the registry.\n\n### Replication Delay Considerations\n\nWhile the search results don't explicitly discuss npm view replication lag timings, they confirm that registry synchronization issues can occur when authentication handshakes fail, potentially causing a package to appear unpublished even after a successful publish command.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."
