[2026-07-19T12:38:01.231Z] [INFO]         "content": "Web search results for query: \"Sentry sourcemaps Node.js ESM no build step not bundled needed\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Source Maps | Sentry for Node.js\",\"url\":\"https://docs.sentry.io/platforms/javascript/guides/node/sourcemaps/\"},{\"title\":\"Better Error Stack Trace with Node.js Source Maps and Sentry\",\"url\":\"https://blog.tericcabrel.com/nodejs-sourcemaps-sentry/\"},{\"title\":\"Source Maps | Sentry for JavaScript\",\"url\":\"https://docs.sentry.io/platforms/javascript/sourcemaps/\"},{\"title\":\"esbuild | Sentry for Node.js\",\"url\":\"https://docs.sentry.io/platforms/javascript/guides/node/sourcemaps/uploading/esbuild/\"},{\"title\":\"Sourcemaps not working for server bundles · Issue #1728 · getsentry/sentry-cli\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-cli/issues/1728\"},{\"title\":\"Troubleshooting Source Maps | Sentry for Node.js\",\"url\":\"https://docs.sentry.io/platforms/javascript/guides/node/sourcemaps/troubleshooting_js/\"},{\"title\":\"Sentry starts sourcemap uploads before NextJS build is finished · Issue #13533 · getsentry/sentry-javascript\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/issues/13533\"},{\"title\":\"Source Maps | Sentry for Express\",\"url\":\"https://docs.sentry.io/platforms/node/guides/express/sourcemaps/\"},{\"title\":\"Troubleshooting Source Maps | Sentry for JavaScript\",\"url\":\"https://docs.sentry.io/platforms/javascript/sourcemaps/troubleshooting_js/\"},{\"title\":\"sentry/esbuild-plugin\",\"url\":\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@sentry/esbuild-plugin\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Sentry sourcemaps for Node.js ESM without a build step:\n\n## Key Information\n\nIf you're not using bundlers like webpack, Vite, Rollup, or Esbuild, Sentry assumes you already know how to generate source maps with your toolchain and recommends uploading them using Sentry CLI.\n\nFor unbundled Node.js ESM applications, the approach differs from bundled code. Service files which aren't bundled can work with source maps, suggesting that Sentry does support sourcemaps for non-bundled code.\n\n## Setup Process\n\nYou can run the wizard with `npx @sentry/wizard@latest -i sourcemaps` and ensure you're running a production build.\n\n## Important Considerations\n\nThe Sentry Node.js SDK generally works well with the source-map-support package if you don't already have source maps uploaded to Sentry. This can be useful for unbundled ESM applications as an alternative to uploading sourcemaps.\n\nThe documentation indicates that for non-bundled setups without build tools like webpack or Esbuild, you should upload source maps using Sentry CLI as the standard approach.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."
