[2026-07-19T12:38:09.569Z] [INFO]         "content": "# Source Maps - Key Points from Sentry Documentation\n\nBased on the provided content, I cannot find specific information addressing your three requested areas:\n\n1. **When source maps are needed** - The page states the general purpose: \"To enable readable stack traces in your Sentry errors, you need to upload your source maps to Sentry.\" However, it doesn't explicitly explain scenarios where they're necessary versus optional.\n\n2. **What happens if code isn't transpiled/bundled** - This scenario is not discussed in the provided material.\n\n3. **Recommendations for plain Node projects without a build step** - The documentation addresses projects using webpack, Vite, Rollup, esbuild, TypeScript, UglifyJS, and SystemJS. For projects outside these tools, it only suggests: \"we recommend you upload them using Sentry CLI.\" There are no specific recommendations for Node projects without build processes.\n\nThe closest relevant guidance is: \"**Note:** Source maps are only generated and uploaded during **production builds**. Development builds typically do not generate source maps for upload.\"\n\nTo get answers to your specific questions, you would likely need to consult additional Sentry documentation sections not included in this excerpt."
