[2026-07-19T12:38:11.468Z] [INFO]         "content": "# chart-releaser-action Overview\n\n**What it does:**\nThis GitHub Action automates Helm chart publishing. It \"turn[s] a GitHub project into a self-hosted Helm chart repo\" by packaging charts, creating GitHub releases, and maintaining an index file on GitHub Pages.\n\n**OCI Support:**\nThe action has limited OCI capability. There's a `skip_upload` option that \"will skip the upload step\" to enable \"more advanced uploading of your charts (for exemple with OCI based repositories) which doen't require the `index.yaml`.\" This suggests OCI workflows require external handling rather than native support.\n\n**Project Status:**\n- **Stars:** 664\n- **Latest Release:** v1.7.0 (January 20, 2025)\n- **Maintenance Status:** Active—recent release indicates ongoing maintenance\n\n**GitHub Pages Requirement:**\nThe README states: \"A GitHub branch called `gh-pages` to store the published charts\" is required, and the action manages this automatically: \"You do not need an `index.yaml` file in `main` at all because it is managed in the `gh-pages` branch.\""
