[2026-07-19T12:38:22.037Z] [INFO]         "content": "Web search results for query: \"github-push-action non-fast-forward retry rebase \"git-auto-commit-action\" push failure concurrent main branch\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Retry for non-fast-forward pushes · Issue #170 · stefanzweifel/git-auto-commit-action\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/stefanzweifel/git-auto-commit-action/issues/170\"},{\"title\":\"Git Rebase Push · Actions · GitHub Marketplace · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/marketplace/actions/git-rebase-push\"},{\"title\":\"Handle failed push error when head falls behind · Issue #209 · stefanzweifel/git-auto-commit-action\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/stefanzweifel/git-auto-commit-action/issues/209\"},{\"title\":\"Automatic Rebase · Actions · GitHub Marketplace · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/marketplace/actions/automatic-rebase\"},{\"title\":\"Git: Force push safely with --force-with-lease and --force-if-includes - Adam Johnson\",\"url\":\"https://adamj.eu/tech/2023/10/31/git-force-push-safely/\"},{\"title\":\"How to Fix 'Push Rejected' Non-Fast-Forward Errors\",\"url\":\"https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-01-24-git-push-rejected-non-fast-forward/view\"},{\"title\":\"Git Push Rejected? Here's Exactly How to Fix a Non-Fast-Forward Error (Fast) - DEV Community\",\"url\":\"https://dev.to/shawon/git-push-rejected-heres-exactly-how-to-fix-a-non-fast-forward-error-fast-4oob\"},{\"title\":\"Auto rebase · Actions · GitHub Marketplace · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/marketplace/actions/auto-rebase\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the topic:\n\n## Non-Fast-Forward Push Issues with git-auto-commit-action\n\nThe git-auto-commit-action should do a pull if it encounters \"non-fast-forward\" as push result and then retry. This is a common problem that occurs in CI/CD workflows.\n\n### The Problem\n\nThis error can crop up if another action has committed since your current action started. When running a build matrix where each job updates another file and you want to have all updates committed, concurrent pushes can cause conflicts.\n\n### Why It Happens\n\nA non-fast-forward push occurs when commits are removed, or \"rewind\", some commits before adding new ones. The non-fast-forward error occurs when the remote branch is not an ancestor of the commit you are trying to push, and often your local branch has diverged from the remote branch with commits you do not have locally.\n\n### Solutions\n\nThe cleanest way to resolve this is a rebase pull followed by a push: `git pull --rebase origin your-branch-name` followed by `git push origin your-branch-name`.\n\nAdditionally, there's a GitHub Action called Git Rebase Push that handles concurrent git commits with automatic rebase retry loop, perfect for GitOps workflows where multiple processes update the same repository simultaneously.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."
