[2026-07-19T12:38:33.472Z] [INFO]         "content": "Web search results for query: \"Helm 3.8.0 release OCI support \"generally available\" graduated experimental\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Release Helm 3.8.0 · helm/helm\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/helm/helm/releases/tag/v3.8.0\"},{\"title\":\"Use OCI-based registries | Helm\",\"url\":\"https://helm.sh/docs/v3/topics/registries/\"},{\"title\":\"helm/helm v3.8.0 on GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://newreleases.io/project/github/helm/helm/release/v3.8.0\"},{\"title\":\"OCI Support | Helm\",\"url\":\"https://helm.sh/community/hips/hip-0006/\"},{\"title\":\"helm-www/versioned_docs/version-3/topics/registries.md at main · helm/helm-www\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/helm/helm-www/blob/main/versioned_docs/version-3/topics/registries.md\"},{\"title\":\"Storing Helm Charts in OCI Registries | Helm\",\"url\":\"https://helm.sh/blog/storing-charts-in-oci/\"},{\"title\":\"Helm | Use OCI-based registries\",\"url\":\"https://docs.helm.sh/docs/topics/registries/\"},{\"title\":\"Deploying Helm Charts from an OCI registry with ArgoCD | simonko.dev - a blog about cloud, kubernetes, containers and more\",\"url\":\"https://simonko.dev/posts/k8s/deploying-helm-charts-from-oci-with-argo/\"},{\"title\":\"Helm OCI MediaType Registration | Helm\",\"url\":\"https://helm.sh/community/hips/hip-0017/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Helm 3.8.0 and OCI support:\n\nOCI registry support for charts is now generally available in Helm 3.8.0 and has graduated out of being an experiment. Beginning in Helm v3.8.0, OCI support is enabled by default.\n\nThis release focused on OCI registries, support for Kubernetes 1.23, and more.\n\nSome key improvements in Helm 3.8.0 included:\n\n- When setting a chart in the dependencies as OCI the version can be set to a range, like other dependencies\n- helm registry login now follows the same structure as the Docker CLI for storing credentials\n- SemVer tags that include build information can be pushed and used\n\nWith the release of Helm 3.8.0, Helm is able to store and work with charts in container registries, as an alternative to Helm repositories, with this feature now generally available after being an experimental feature.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."
