[2026-07-19T12:38:43.404Z] [INFO]         "content": "Web search results for query: \"npm/cli issue \"just published\" package not found \"npm view\" immediately after publish delay github issue\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"npm publish 404 Not Found - PUT · Issue #1637 · npm/cli\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/npm/cli/issues/1637\"},{\"title\":\"[BUG] npm is not finding newly published versions of packages · Issue #3424 · npm/cli\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/npm/cli/issues/3424\"},{\"title\":\"When will my published repo be available in the npm registry? · community · Discussion #46463\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/orgs/community/discussions/46463\"},{\"title\":\"[BUG] After `npm publish`, `npm pack` cannot find the package · Issue #9043 · npm/cli\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/npm/cli/issues/9043\"},{\"title\":\"[BUG] Npm publish failed, file not found · Issue #7853 · npm/cli\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/npm/cli/issues/7853\"},{\"title\":\"[BUG] Can't publish package · Issue #6260 · npm/cli\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/npm/cli/issues/6260\"},{\"title\":\"[BUG] NPM Publish seems to not read package.json's publishConfig · Issue #6939 · npm/cli\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/npm/cli/issues/6939\"},{\"title\":\"New version of pkg is published but not getting shown · Issue #593 · npm/cli\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/npm/cli/issues/593\"},{\"title\":\"[BUG] regression, `npm publish folder` has a new and completely incompatible behaviour where `folder` is interpreted as a package name and is then fetched from the registry · Issue #4126 · npm/cli\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/npm/cli/issues/4126\"}]\n\nI found several relevant GitHub issues related to npm publish and package availability delays. Here are some key findings:\n\nOne issue (#3424) reports that after publishing a package with `npm publish`, users encounter an error \"No matching version found\" when trying to install the newly published version immediately afterward.\n\nAnother issue (#9043) describes a similar problem where users add a retry system (5 times every minute) after publishing, but the tarball is still not found even after 5 minutes.\n\nAccording to npm documentation, it can typically take a few minutes for a package to be fully processed and available in the npm registry after running `npm publish`.\n\nA longer-standing issue (#593) from 2019 reported that after publishing version 3.3.1 of the chokidar package, the npm page, curl JSON API, and npm all only showed version 3.3.0 as available.\n\nThese issues indicate a common problem where newly published npm packages are not immediately available for installation or viewing via `npm view`, which appears to be a known delay issue in the npm registry system.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."
