[2026-07-19T12:45:57.924Z] [INFO]           "prompt": "Repo: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784463865325, branch issue-2082-90c17c1e7d2a. Work ONLY on the files listed below — another agent and I are editing scripts/, .github/workflows/, and dev/log/ concurrently. DO NOT touch those, DO NOT commit, DO NOT push. Leave changes in the working tree and report what you did.\n\nCONTEXT (issue #2082 — finding F21): the `tests/` directory (358 files) is entirely excluded from ESLint. `package.json` `lint` script only globs `src/**`, `scripts/**`, `eslint-rules/**`, and the config block in `eslint.config.mjs` that defines Node globals + rules has `files: ['src/**/*.{js,mjs,cjs}', 'scripts/**/*.{js,mjs,cjs}', 'eslint-rules/**/*.{js,mjs,cjs}']`. Because `js.configs.recommended` still applies `no-undef` globally but the globals block does not cover tests/, linting tests/ today reports 4,621 errors — ~4,450 of which are phantom `'console' is not defined` / `'process' is not defined`.\n\nYOUR TASK:\n1. Add `'tests/**/*.{js,mjs,cjs}'` to the `files:` array at eslint.config.mjs line ~99. Verify this drops `npx eslint tests/` from 4621 to ~174 problems.\n2. Fix the ~172 remaining REAL errors in tests/ so that `npx eslint tests/` is clean. Breakdown: 67 no-unused-vars, 55 camelcase, 11 timers/no-leaked-timers, 10 gh-rate-limit/no-direct-gh-exec, 8 no-useless-assignment, 8 preserve-caught-error, 7 no-regex-spaces, 2 no-prototype-builtins, 1 each of prettier/prettier, no-empty, gh-paginate/require-gh-paginate, no-constant-condition, no-constant-binary-expression, no-useless-escape.\n3. Add `'tests/**/*.{js,mjs,cjs}'` to the `lint` and `lint:fix` scripts in package.json so CI actually checks tests going forward.\n\nCRITICAL RULES:\n- These are TESTS. A \"fix\" that weakens or deletes an assertion is unacceptable. Never delete a test, never comment one out, never change what an assertion checks.\n- For `no-unused-vars`: prefer removing genuinely dead variables. If a variable is a deliberately-unused function parameter, rename it with a leading `_` (the config sets argsIgnorePattern/varsIgnorePattern to '^_'). Do NOT add eslint-disable comments as a shortcut.\n- For `camelcase`: many of these will be legitimate API-shaped fixture data (e.g. `pull_request`, `head_ref`, `created_at`) matching GitHub's JSON. These MUST keep their snake_case names — changing them would break the fixture's fidelity to the real API. For those, the correct fix is a narrowly-scoped eslint-disable with a comment explaining it mirrors the GitHub API schema, OR check whether the config's `properties: 'never'` already exempts object properties (it should — so only standalone variable/binding names should be erroring). Investigate before changing anything.\n- For `timers/no-leaked-timers`, `gh-rate-limit/no-direct-gh-exec`, `gh-paginate/require-gh-paginate`: these are the repo's OWN custom correctness rules (see eslint-rules/). Read each rule's implementation to understand what it wants. These 22 may be real latent bugs in the tests — report any that look like genuine defects rather than style nits.\n- For `preserve-caught-error`: the modern fix is `throw new Error('msg', { cause: err })`.\n- After every batch of edits, re-run the affected test files with `node tests/<file>` to confirm they still pass. Tests are plain node scripts using node:assert.\n- Run `node scripts/run-tests.mjs --suite default` at the end if it completes in reasonable time, and report the result.\n\nReport: what you changed by category, any genuine bugs found in tests, any errors you could NOT fix cleanly and why, and confirmation that `npx eslint tests/` is clean and tests still pass.",
