es/2082/pulls/2083/ci-logs/*.log.gz -diff\n     dev/log/issues/2082/pulls/2083/analysis/*.log.txt -diff\n     ```\n\n   - **`eslint.config.mjs`** — line 99 is the key line (currently UNMODIFIED by me — I reverted my experiment; a background agent is now editing it):\n     ```js\n     files: ['src/**/*.{js,mjs,cjs}', 'scripts/**/*.{js,mjs,cjs}', 'eslint-rules/**/*.{js,mjs,cjs}'],\n     ```\n     Adding `'tests/**/*.{js,mjs,cjs}'` drops `npx eslint tests/` from 4,621 → 174 problems.\n\n   - **`package.json`** lines 20–25:\n     ```\n     \"test\": \"node scripts/run-tests.mjs --suite default\",\n     \"lint\": \"eslint 'src/**/*.{js,mjs,cjs}' 'scripts/**/*.{js,mjs,cjs}' 'eslint-rules/**/*.{js,mjs,cjs}'\",\n     \"lint:fix\": \"eslint '...' --fix\",\n     ```\n\n   - **`scripts/publish-to-npm.mjs`** — READ (not yet modified). F5 defect at lines 145–181: `publishWithRetry` calls `isVersionPublished` immediately with no backoff, and on a false-negative verification re-invokes the **entire** `npm run changeset:publish` rather than merely re-polling.\n\n   - **`scripts/publish-failure-classifier.mjs`** — READ. `FAILURE_PATTERNS` = ['packages failed to publish', 'error occurred while publishing', 'npm error code e', 'npm error 404', 'npm error 401', 'npm error 403', 'access token expired', 'eneedauth', 'cannot find module', 'module_not_found']. `NON_RETRYABLE_PATTERNS` = ['npm error 404', 'npm error 401', 'npm error 403', 'e404', 'e401', 'e403', 'access token expired', 'eneedauth', 'you must be logged in', 'unable to authenticate'].\n\n   - **`tests/test-publish-to-npm-2028.mjs`** — READ (header). Imports `{ analyzePublishResult, publishWithRetry, runPublishFlow, isVersionPublished, PACKAGE_NAME }`. Uses a `test(name, fn)` helper with ✅/❌ and passed/failed counters, `noSleep`, `quietLogger`, `VERSION = '2.1.10'`.\n\n4. **Errors and fixes:**\n   - **`jq: command not found` (exit 127)** (from earlier session) — jq unavailable; worked around with `tr`/`grep`/`gh --json` field selection and inline `node -e`. Must continue avoiding `jq`.\n   - **Shell cwd persistence** — `cd dev/log/...` in one Bash call persisted into the next, causing `cd: No such file or directory` on a repeated relative `cd`. Fixed by using absolute paths.\n   - **`npx eslint` failed with `Cannot find package '@eslint/js'`** — `node_modules` was missing. Fixed by running `npm ci` (exit 0).\n   - **`'console' is not defined  no-undef` in `tests/helm-release-2082.test.mjs`** — NOT a defect in my file; it exposed finding F21 (tests/ excluded from the ESLint globals scope). Left as-is for the moment; delegated the systematic fix.\n   - **`*.log` is gitignored**, blocking the user's \"compile that data into the folder\" requirement. Fixed by following repo precedent (commit `b7d83567`, `.gitattributes` `-diff` entries): gzipped the two large CI logs (8.8 MB → 1.4 MB) and renamed small excerpts to `.log.txt` (matching `docs/case-studies/issue-2080/raw/*.log.txt`).\n   - No user corrections or feedback have been received (only one user turn exists).\n\n5. **Problem Solving:**\n\n   **F1 (CRITICAL) — SOLVED, FIXED, TESTED, COMMITTED, PUSHED.** Helm release publishes nothing while reporting success. Proven chain: gh-pages carries the repo tree → script rewrites `helm/hive-mind/Chart.yaml` → `git checkout gh-pages` aborts → `$` swallows it → execution continues on main → commit lands on main (`[main f723e208]`) → `git push origin gh-pages` = \"Everything up-to-date\" → `git checkout -` fails → prints \"released successfully!\", exit 0. Production proof: published `index.yaml` newest entry is 0.38.8 (2025-12-11); package.json at 2.8.3. Regression origin: commit `5b7e60d7` (2025-12-23) replaced `helm-release.sh` (which had `set -euo pipefail`) with the `.mjs` version.\n\n   **Mutation test validated the fix's test.** Replacing `runStrict` with the soft runner in `helm-release.lib.mjs` made the test fail with `AssertionError: Missing expected rejection: a failing git command must abort the release instead of falling through to \"released successfully\"`. Restoring the fix made it pass. This is direct evidence the test catches the exact production regression.\n\n   **Committed as `ba3c57a4`** with a detailed conventional-commit message documenting root cause, evidence, and every change. **Pushed** (`efe9d369..ba3c57a4`).\n\n   **Research completed (user request #2, \"check online for known existing components/libraries\").** Key corrections to my plan:\n   - `execa`/`zx`/`dax` all **throw by default** — command-stream is the outlier `[VERIFIED for execa & zx]`\n   - **Neither zizmor nor actionlint has a `timeout-minutes` audit** — zizmor #1023 and actionlint #49 are both OPEN `[VERIFIED negative]`. This *disproved* a false search-engine summary. → porting `ci-timeouts.test.js` as a custom check is correct.\n   - **Caveat for that check:** jobs calling a reusable workflow via `uses:` do **not** support `timeout-minutes` — a naive assertion would create a NEW false positive.\n   - **npm publish:** no verification tool exists; the `npm ≥11.5.1` OIDC-404 red herring must be ruled out before assuming replication lag.\n   - **Sentry:** docs never address the no-build-step case → remove the step.\n   - **Helm:** `helm/chart-releaser-action` or OCI/GHCR are the off-the-shelf options; decision recorded to fix in place (gh-pages contract is a user-facing API) and defer migration to a follow-up issue.\n\n   **NEW finding F21 discovered:** `tests/` (358 files) is entirely excluded from ESLint — `package.json`'s lint script doesn't glob it AND `eslint.config.mjs:99`'s `files:` array omits it. 4,621 reported errors collapse to 174 real ones once globals are scoped correctly. Of those 174, **22 are violations of the repo's own custom correctness rules** (`timers/no-leaked-timers` × 11, `gh-rate-limit/no-direct-gh-exec` × 10, `gh-paginate/require-gh-paginate` × 1) that tests were escaping — potentially latent bugs, not style nits.\n\n   **F5 (in progress, analysis stage).** Re-read the production log excerpt to pin the sequence: attempt 1 publishes successfully + creates tag v2.8.3 → immediate `npm view` returns E404 → verifier declares failure → attempt 2 re-runs full `changeset publish` → \"You cannot publish over the previously published versions: 2.8.3\" → \"Publish attempt 2 failed: exit code 1\" → attempt 3 → \"Verified @link-assistant/hive-mind@2.8.3 is live on npm\". Green only by luck of the 3-attempt budget. I had just noticed a subtlety worth confirming: the attempt-2 EPUBLISHCONFLICT did **not** trip `NON_RETRYABLE_PATTERNS` (the log shows a plain \"exit code 1\" failure, not the non-retryable early return with auth guidance), so changeset's rendering of that error apparently lacks the literal `e403`/`npm error 403` strings. This matters for designing the fix.\n\n   **Two background agents:**\n   - Research agent (aeee2e46535a466d6) — COMPLETED, results saved and incorporated.\n   - Tests-lint-cleanup agent (a48b7675bdca78e23) — **STILL RUNNING**. Instructed to edit only `eslint.config.mjs`, `package.json` lint scripts, and `tests/**`; explicitly told NOT to touch `scripts/`, `.github/workflows/`, `dev/log/`, and NOT to commit or push. Given strict rules: never weaken/delete assertions, prefer `_` prefix for deliberately-unused params, investigate camelcase cases (GitHub-API-shaped fixtures must keep snake_case), read the custom rules' implementations, re-run affected tests after each batch.\n\n6. **All user messages:**\n\n   There has been exactly **one** user message — the initial task prompt (captured in the provided context summary). Its verbatim key constraints:\n   - \"Download all logs and collect data related about the issue to this repository, and compile that data into the ./dev/log/issues/2082/pulls/2083 folder.\"\n   - \"Use the collected evidence to do a deep analysis (search online for additional facts and data), reconstruct the timeline/sequence of events, list each and every requirement from the issue, find the root cause of each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement. Also check online for known existing components/libraries that solve a similar problem or can help.\"\n   - \"If there is not enough data to find the actual root cause, add debug output and a verbose mode (if not already present) so the root cause can be found on the next iteration. Keep the default state switched off.\"\n   - \"If the issue is related to another repository/project, report issues on GitHub for that project when possible. Each report must contain reproducible examples, workarounds, and suggestions for fixing the issue in code.\"\n   - \"Double-check that the requirements are fully applied to the entire codebase: if an issue exists in multiple places, apply it in all of them.\"\n   - \"Proceed.\"\n\n   No further user messages have been received. All subsequent items in the transcript were automated `<task-notification>` background-task events, each explicitly stating they are NOT user input and must NOT be treated as approval or consent.\n\n7. **Pending Tasks:**\n   1. **F5** — fix npm publish retry granularity in `scripts/publish-to-npm.mjs`: poll `isVersionPublished` with backoff instead of re-running `changeset:publish`; treat same-version `EPUBLISHCONFLICT` as success; check the publish job's npm version against the ≥11.5.1 OIDC caveat. Write the reproducing test first (extend `tests/test-publish-to-npm-2028.mjs` or add a new `-2082` test).\n   2. **F4** — `scripts/version-and-commit.mjs:219` bare `await $\\`git push origin main\\`` → use `runStrict` + rebase-retry.\n   3. **F7** — split the four files sitting at exactly 1500/1500 lines (`src/solve.mjs`, `src/claude.lib.mjs`, `src/codex.lib.mjs`, `src/telegram-solve-queue.lib.mjs`).\n   4. **F6** — add `timeout-minutes` to all ~26 jobs in both workflows; port `tests/ci-timeouts.test.js` (mind the reusable-workflow `uses:` caveat).\n   5. **F3** — de-vacuum `scripts/test-auto-fork-option.sh`, `test-global-commands.sh`, `verify-log-file-contents.sh` (and `release.yml:359,369`); leave the two `npm unlink -g … || true` trap-cleanup lines alone.\n   6. **F8** — `check-mjs-syntax.sh` to cover `scripts/`, add missing `timeout 10s` on the tests loop.\n   7. **F9** — add `.secretlintrc.json` + CI step.\n   8. **F13/F14** — `always()` → `!cancelled()` (10 jobs); adopt template concurrency (`!= main` + non-cancellable `main-writer` group).\n   9. **F10** — `npm pkg fix` for the `bin` `./` prefixes.\n   10. **F11** — remove the Sentry sourcemap step (research says it's meaningless with no build step).\n   11. **F12/F15–F20** — jscpd ignores + threshold, `allowScripts` decision, `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/KEY_0/VALUE_0`, `NODE_OPTIONS=--no-deprecation`, drop `--force` from Dockerfiles, bump actions `@v5`→`@v6`.\n   12. **F21** — tests/ ESLint coverage (delegated, in progress).\n   13. **R7 docs** — add timeout + cancellation sections to `docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md` and its `zh`/`hi`/`ru` translations.\n   14. **R6 upstream** — file issue(s) on `link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template` (it lacks hive-mind's `detectPublishFailure()`/`FAILURE_PATTERNS` hardening from #2028), with reproducible example + workaround + suggested code fix. Also possibly the F5 publish/verify race, pending confirmation the template shares that structure.\n   15. Add analysis docs for the remaining findings (F4–F21) to `dev/log/issues/2082/pulls/2083/analysis/`.\n   16. Add a changeset / version bump for release.\n   17. Merge `main` into the branch; run full local CI; update PR 2083 via `gh pr edit`; verify CI green; `gh pr ready 2083`; confirm clean `git status`.\n\n8. **Current Work:**\n\n   I had just committed and pushed the F1 fix (`ba3c57a4`), launched the tests-lint background agent, and moved on to **F5 — the npm publish double-publish race**, following the user's \"create a test that reproduces the problem, then implement the fix\" requirement.\n\n   I had read the header of `tests/test-publish-to-npm-2028.mjs` (to match its existing `test(name, fn)` / ✅❌ style) and `scripts/publish-failure-classifier.mjs` (to learn `FAILURE_PATTERNS` and `NON_RETRYABLE_PATTERNS`), then grepped the saved production evidence:\n\n   ```\n   grep -n -i \"attempt\\|cannot publish\\|E404\\|EPUBLISHCONFLICT\\|403\\|Verified\\|success packages\" \\\n     dev/log/issues/2082/pulls/2083/analysis/npm-publish-race-excerpt.log.txt\n   ```\n   which returned:\n   ```\n   13:  npm error code E404\n   22:  Publish attempt 1 of 3...\n   36:  🦋  Creating git tag...\n   39:  npm error code E404\n   49:  Publish attempt 2 of 3...\n   61:  🦋  error an error occurred while publishing @link-assistant/hive-mind: undefined You cannot publish over the previously published versi\n   79:  🦋  error npm error You cannot publish over the previously published versions: 2.8.3.\n   84:  Publish attempt 2 failed: exit code 1\n   86:  Publish attempt 3 of 3...\n   100: Verified @link-assistant/hive-mind@2.8.3 is live on npm\n   ```\n\n   The fix design (recorded in `F0-existing-solutions-research.md`) is: *\"the current code's defect is not that it verifies — verification is the #2028 protection and must stay — it is the **retry granularity**: a failed verification re-runs the entire `changeset:publish`. Fix = poll verification with backoff, never republish after a publish that reported success, and treat a same-version `EPUBLISHCONFLICT` as success.\"*\n\n   The specific code to change is `publishWithRetry` in `scripts/publish-to-npm.mjs:145–181`, where:\n   ```js\n   const published = await isVersionPublished(runner, version);   // line 157 — immediate, no backoff\n   if (published) { return { ok: true, attempt }; }\n   lastReason = 'post-publish verification failed: version not found on npm';\n   ```\n   falls through to the top of the `for` loop, which re-runs `await runner('npm', ['run', 'changeset:publish'])`.\n\n9. **Optional Next Step:**\n\n   Write the reproducing test for F5 (a new `tests/publish-verification-backoff-2082.test.mjs` or an extension of `tests/test-publish-to-npm-2028.mjs`) asserting that after a publish reports success, a transiently-404ing registry is **re-polled with backoff** and `changeset:publish` is invoked **exactly once** — then implement the `publishWithRetry` change in `scripts/publish-to-npm.mjs`, and mutation-check it the same way I validated the F1 test.\n\n   This is directly in line with what I was doing immediately before the summary request. My stated plan for this item, verbatim from the committed research doc: *\"Fix = poll verification with backoff, never republish after a publish that reported success, and treat a same-version `EPUBLISHCONFLICT` as success. Also check the runner's npm version against the OIDC caveat above.\"* And from the master README's solution plan: *\"**F5** — split retry granularity: poll `isVersionPublished` with backoff instead of re-running `changeset:publish`; treat `EPUBLISHCONFLICT` for the same version as success.\"*\n\n   Note: the background agent `a48b7675bdca78e23` (tests/ ESLint cleanup) is still running and has uncommitted changes in the working tree to `eslint.config.mjs`, `package.json`, and `tests/**` — avoid touching those files until it reports, and do not commit while it is mid-edit.\n</summary>');\n       return new RegExp(`^\\\\s*-?\\\\s*version:\\\\s*[\"']?${escaped}[\"']?\\\\s*\n\n, 'm').test(indexYaml);\n     }\n     ```\n     - `releaseHelmChart` flow: `strict('git', ['config', ...])` → update Chart.yaml → `helm lint` → `helm package` → assert archive exists → soft `git ls-remote --exit-code --heads origin gh-pages` (create via `git commit-tree` + push if absent) → `git fetch origin +refs/heads/gh-pages:refs/remotes/origin/gh-pages` → **try**: `git worktree add --force -B gh-pages <dir> origin/gh-pages`, `fs.copyFileSync(archivePath, worktree/archive)`, `helm repo index <dir> --url <url> [--merge <dir>/index.yaml]`, `git -C <dir> add -f -