[2026-07-19T12:51:37.047Z] [INFO]           "command": "git add scripts/publish-to-npm.mjs scripts/publish-failure-classifier.mjs tests/publish-verification-race-2082.test.mjs && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfix(ci): stop the npm publish/verify race republishing a live version (#2082)\n\nFinding F5 of issue #2082. Reproduced by tests/publish-verification-race-2082.test.mjs,\nwhich fails against the previous implementation.\n\nRoot cause: retry granularity. `publishWithRetry` verified the version with a\nsingle `npm view` immediately after publishing, and on a miss fell through to the\ntop of the retry loop — re-running the entire `npm run changeset:publish`. But the\nnpm registry serves metadata through a CDN, so a version can be invisible to\n`npm view` for seconds after publish returns success (npm/cli#3424, #9043, #593).\nA verification miss is therefore not evidence that the publish failed.\n\nObserved in CI run 29647956700, a run that went GREEN:\n\n    14:38:40  Publish attempt 1 of 3...\n    14:38:46  success packages published successfully: @link-assistant/hive-mind@2.8.3\n    14:38:46  Creating git tag... New tag: v2.8.3\n    14:38:46  npm error code E404                       <- verified 0.3s after publish\n    14:38:56  Publish attempt 2 of 3...                 <- re-ran the whole publish\n    14:38:59  error npm error You cannot publish over the previously published versions: 2.8.3.\n    14:39:09  Publish attempt 3 of 3...\n    14:39:10  Verified @link-assistant/hive-mind@2.8.3 is live on npm\n\nThe release had already succeeded on attempt 1. It went green only because a\nthird attempt fit inside the budget, and only because by then there were no\nchangesets left for attempt 3 to publish. With one more second of CDN lag, or\none fewer retry, a completed release would have been reported as a failure.\n\nChanges:\n  - waitForVersionOnRegistry(): polls `npm view` with exponential backoff\n    (2s -> 30s, ~90s total) instead of checking once.\n  - A publish that reported success is never re-run. If verification ultimately\n    fails the job fails — the #2028 false-positive protection is unchanged — but\n    it fails on the verification, not by publishing again.\n  - isVersionConflict(output, version): recognises npm's EPUBLISHCONFLICT for the\n    version being released and treats it as \"already landed\", still subject to\n    verification so a false claim cannot turn into a green release. Matched\n    before the non-retryable classifier, since npm reports the conflict with a\n    403 that would otherwise be misread as an auth failure.\n  - Genuine publish failures are still retried exactly as before.\n\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1",
