[2026-07-19T12:54:47.709Z] [INFO]         "input": {
[2026-07-19T12:54:47.709Z] [INFO]           "command": "npx prettier --write scripts/version-and-commit.mjs scripts/version-and-commit.lib.mjs tests/version-and-commit-2082.test.mjs >/dev/null 2>&1\ngit add scripts/version-and-commit.mjs scripts/version-and-commit.lib.mjs tests/version-and-commit-2082.test.mjs && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfix(ci): fail the release when the version bump is not pushed to main (#2082)\n\nFinding F4 of issue #2082 — the same fail-soft defect as F1, with a worse\nconsequence. Reproduced by tests/version-and-commit-2082.test.mjs, which fails\nagainst the previous implementation.\n\nRoot cause: scripts/version-and-commit.mjs ran every git command as a bare\n`await $\\`...\\``. command-stream's `$` resolves with `.code` instead of throwing,\nso the try/catch wrapping main() could never fire.\n\n`git push origin main` is racy by construction: the release workflow pushes the\nversion bump to main while merges and other runs push to the same branch. When\nthe push was rejected as non-fast-forward, the rejection was swallowed — the\nscript printed \"Version bump committed and pushed to main\", set\n`version_committed=true`, and exited 0. The downstream publish job then worked\nfrom a version that existed only in the runner's local checkout. Every command\nbefore the push had the same problem: a failed `npm run changeset:version` or\n`git commit` continued straight on to the push.\n\nChanges:\n  - scripts/version-and-commit.lib.mjs: the logic, extracted with injectable\n    runner/output/logger so it can be unit-tested, with every command run\n    through `runStrict` (restoring `set -e` semantics).\n  - pushWithRebaseRetry(): a rejected push is rebased onto the new remote HEAD\n    and retried (5 attempts, 3s apart) rather than assumed to have won the race.\n    isNonFastForward() distinguishes a lost race from auth/network/protected-\n    branch failures, which are not fixed by rebasing and so fail immediately\n    with the real error.\n  - `version_committed=true` is emitted only after a push that actually landed.\n  - scripts/version-and-commit.mjs is now a thin argument-parsing CLI and no\n    longer imports command-stream.\n\nVerified by mutation: restoring the fail-soft runner makes the test fail with\n\"Missing expected rejection: a failing version bump must abort instead of\ncontinuing to commit and push\"; replacing the retry with a single push makes the\nrejected-push case fail. Both are the production defects.\n\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && git push origin issue-2082-90c17c1e7d2a 2>&1 | tail -2",
