[2026-07-19T12:57:56.554Z] [INFO]           "command": "npx eslint scripts/workflow-lint.lib.mjs && npx prettier --write scripts/workflow-lint.lib.mjs tests/ci-workflow-timeouts-2082.test.mjs >/dev/null 2>&1\ngit add .github/workflows/ scripts/workflow-lint.lib.mjs tests/ci-workflow-timeouts-2082.test.mjs && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfix(ci): require timeout-minutes on every job and enforce it in tests (#2082)\n\nFinding F6 of issue #2082. 22 of the 26 jobs across the two workflows had no\n`timeout-minutes`, so each inherited GitHub's 360-minute default: a job that\nhangs on a prompt, a dead socket or a runaway test burns six hours of runner\ntime and then surfaces as a generic failure that looks nothing like a hang.\ndocs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md already required an explicit timeout; nothing\nenforced it.\n\nTimeouts were chosen from measured job durations across the last four successful\nrelease runs (29685608578, 29686630893, 29686761617, 29686947280) rather than\nguessed. Observed maxima: test-suites 11m, Docker DinD amd64 7m, Docker amd64\n6m, everything else under 2m. Applied limits give roughly 2-3x headroom\n(test-suites 30, Docker merge jobs 30, release/instant-release 30, most checks\n10-15). The four matrix Docker jobs already had 60 and are unchanged.\n\nEnforcement lives in tests/ci-workflow-timeouts-2082.test.mjs, backed by\nscripts/workflow-lint.lib.mjs. Nothing off the shelf does this: the zizmor\nrequest (zizmorcore/zizmor#1023) and the actionlint request (rhysd/actionlint#49)\nare both still open, so this is a custom check until one of them ships.\n\nTwo correctness details the check gets right, both of which would otherwise\ntrade one false result for another:\n  - Jobs that call a reusable workflow via `uses:` are exempt. GitHub does not\n    support `timeout-minutes` there; the timeout must live in the called\n    workflow. Demanding one would be a false positive.\n  - A `uses:` on a *step* is an action, not a reusable-workflow call, so it must\n    not exempt the job. Confusing the two would silently exempt nearly every job\n    in this repository.\n\nThe scanner is line-based rather than a YAML parse because js-yaml is only a\ntransitive dependency here and these checks must survive an unknown\nnode_modules state — the same constraint that shaped scripts/run-command.lib.mjs.\nThe result was cross-checked against a real YAML parse: 26 jobs, none missing.\n\nThe test also guards against passing vacuously, asserting both that workflow\nfiles were found and that jobs were actually parsed.\n\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && git push origin issue-2082-90c17c1e7d2a 2>&1 | tail -2",
