[2026-07-19T13:00:37.472Z] [INFO]         "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent:**\n\n   There has been exactly **one** genuine user message in this entire task (the initial prompt; every subsequent item was an automated background-task notification explicitly flagged as NOT user input and NOT approval). The user is operating an AI issue solver on:\n   - **Repo/working dir:** `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784463865325` (link-assistant/hive-mind)\n   - **Branch (push ONLY to this):** `issue-2082-90c17c1e7d2a`\n   - **Issue:** https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2082 — *\"Check for all false positives, false negatives, warnings and errors in CI/CD and fix them all\"*\n   - **PR (already exists — update via `gh pr edit`, do NOT create new):** https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/2083\n\n   Explicit deliverables from the user message:\n   1. \"Download all logs and collect data related about the issue to this repository, and compile that data into the `./dev/log/issues/2082/pulls/2083` folder.\"\n   2. \"Use the collected evidence to do a deep analysis (search online for additional facts and data), reconstruct the timeline/sequence of events, list each and every requirement from the issue, find the root cause of each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement. Also check online for known existing components/libraries that solve a similar problem or can help.\"\n   3. \"If there is not enough data to find the actual root cause, add debug output and a verbose mode (if not already present) so the root cause can be found on the next iteration. Keep the default state switched off.\"\n   4. \"If the issue is related to another repository/project, report issues on GitHub for that project when possible. Each report must contain reproducible examples, workarounds, and suggestions for fixing the issue in code.\"\n   5. \"Double-check that the requirements are fully applied to the entire codebase: if an issue exists in multiple places, apply it in all of them.\"\n   6. \"Proceed.\"\n\n   Requirements derived from issue #2082 itself:\n   - **R1** Find & fix all CI/CD **false positives** (green checks verifying nothing)\n   - **R2** Find & fix all CI/CD **false negatives** (real failures reported as success)\n   - **R3** Find & fix all CI/CD **warnings**\n   - **R4** Find & fix all CI/CD **errors**\n   - **R5** Compare the **full file tree** against `https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template` and reuse all best practices\n   - **R6** \"if the same issue is found in template report issue also in templates\" → file upstream issues\n   - **R7** Follow `docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md`\n   - **R8** \"plan and execute everything in this single pull request … until it is each and every requirement fully addressed\"\n\n   Standing operational constraints from the user message (must persist): commit atomic steps to the branch; **create reproducing tests BEFORE fixes**; keep debug/experiment scripts in `./experiments` and real-world use cases in `./examples`; save large command output to files; run local CI checks (lint etc.) before pushing; download CI logs to `ci-logs/` and Read them; use `gh pr edit` to update PR 2083 and `gh pr ready 2083` when finished; verify clean `git status` at the end; merge default branch into the PR branch; check all three GitHub comment API endpoints (`/pulls/N/comments`, `/issues/N/comments`, `/pulls/N/reviews`) with `--paginate`.\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts:**\n   - **`command-stream`'s `\n\n**: fail-soft — resolves with `.code` instead of throwing. THE root-cause mechanism for F1 and F4; makes wrapping try/catch decorative.\n   - **`set -euo pipefail`** semantics restored in JS via a `runStrict` wrapper over `node:child_process.spawn`.\n   - **Mutation testing as validation**: after every fix, re-introduce the defect and confirm the new test fails with the expected message. Applied to F1, F5, and F4 (twice).\n   - **npm registry CDN propagation lag** → E404 immediately after a successful publish (npm/cli#3424, #9043, #593); plus the **npm ≥11.5.1 OIDC Trusted-Publishing 404 red herring** (a failed OIDC handshake surfaces as a misleading 404 — a retry loop never fixes it).\n   - **npm `EPUBLISHCONFLICT`** — \"You cannot publish over the previously published versions: X\" — reported with a 403, so it must be classified *before* the non-retryable auth classifier.\n   - **Non-fast-forward push rejection** → rebase-and-retry, distinguished from auth/network/protected-branch failures which rebasing cannot fix.\n   - **GitHub Actions `timeout-minutes`**: absent → inherits the 360-minute default. **Not supported on jobs that call a reusable workflow via `uses:`** (job-level), while a *step-level* `uses:` is an action and does NOT exempt the job. Neither zizmor (#1023) nor actionlint (#49) enforces this — both requests still open.\n   - **`git worktree`** publishing; Git's empty-tree hash `4b825dc642cb6eb9a060e54bf8d69288fbee4904` + `git commit-tree`.\n   - **ESLint flat config** `files:` scoping; **lint-staged + prettier** pre-commit hook (auto-reformats staged files — expect quote normalization).\n   - `use-m` dynamic package loading, `lino-arguments` config, `@hive-mind-test-suite default` test annotation (how `scripts/run-tests.mjs --suite default` discovers tests).\n   - **js-yaml is only a transitive dependency** in this repo — not safe to depend on in checks that must survive an unknown `node_modules` state.\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections:**\n\n   **Committed this session — `02498ca3` (F5):**\n\n   - **`scripts/publish-failure-classifier.mjs`** — MODIFIED, added before `buildAuthFailureGuidance`:\n     ```js\n     export function isVersionConflict(output, version) {\n       if (!version) {\n         return false;\n       }\n       const matches = String(output || '').matchAll(/cannot publish over the previously published versions?:\\s*(\\S+)/gi);\n       for (const match of matches) {\n         // The message ends in a full stop: \"...versions: 2.8.3.\"\n         if (match[1].replace(/[.,]+$/, '') === version) {\n           return true;\n         }\n       }\n       return false;\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`scripts/publish-to-npm.mjs`** — MODIFIED. New constants and the import:\n     ```js\n     import { detectPublishFailure, isNonRetryableFailure, isVersionConflict, buildAuthFailureGuidance } from './publish-failure-classifier.mjs';\n     const DEFAULT_VERIFY_ATTEMPTS = 7;\n     const DEFAULT_VERIFY_DELAY_MS = 2000;\n     const DEFAULT_VERIFY_MAX_DELAY_MS = 30000;   // ~2+4+8+16+30+30 = 90s total\n     ```\n     New export:\n     ```js\n     export async function waitForVersionOnRegistry({ runner, version, attempts = DEFAULT_VERIFY_ATTEMPTS, delayMs = DEFAULT_VERIFY_DELAY_MS, maxDelayMs = DEFAULT_VERIFY_MAX_DELAY_MS, sleeper = sleep, logger = console }) {\n       let delay = delayMs;\n       for (let attempt = 1; attempt <= attempts; attempt++) {\n         if (await isVersionPublished(runner, version)) {\n           logger.log(`Verified ${PACKAGE_NAME}@${version} is live on npm (check ${attempt} of ${attempts})`);\n           return true;\n         }\n         if (attempt < attempts) {\n           logger.log(`${PACKAGE_NAME}@${version} not visible yet (check ${attempt} of ${attempts}); waiting ${delay / 1000}s for registry propagation...`);\n           await sleeper(delay);\n           delay = Math.min(delay * 2, maxDelayMs);\n         }\n       }\n       return false;\n     }\n     ```\n     Rewritten `publishWithRetry` core (signature unchanged):\n     ```js\n     const verify = () => waitForVersionOnRegistry({ runner, version, sleeper, logger });\n     const verificationFailed = `post-publish verification failed: ${PACKAGE_NAME}@${version} never appeared on npm`;\n     // ...inside