[2026-07-19T13:09:55.665Z] [INFO]           "command": "cd /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784463865325; git add scripts/shell-lint.lib.mjs tests/shell-script-assertions-2082.test.mjs scripts/test-auto-fork-option.sh scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh scripts/verify-docker-image.sh && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF' && git push -q origin issue-2082-90c17c1e7d2a && git log --oneline -1\nfix(ci): make shell test assertions fail the build, and enforce it (#2082)\n\nscripts/test-auto-fork-option.sh reported none of its three assertions:\neach failed branch printed \"Could not verify ...\" and the script carried\non to exit 0.\n\nThis was not a latent risk. The marker the dry-run checks grep for first\nappears ~32s into the run, because solve.mjs makes several GitHub API\ncalls before reaching the auto-fork decision — and the script killed the\ncommand with `timeout 10s`. Both greps had been failing on every run\nwhile the job stayed green. Reproduced locally: restoring the 10s\ntimeout now fails the script with exactly those two checks red.\n\n- test-auto-fork-option.sh: realistic timeouts, every check asserts, and\n  a hermetic --help check that does not depend on the network.\n- check-file-line-limits.sh: a missing release.yml was a warning that\n  skipped the check entirely; it is now an error.\n- scripts/shell-lint.lib.mjs + tests: flag any `else` branch that reports\n  a failure without failing. Branches that record the failure for a later\n  check are exempt; deliberately non-fatal ones must say so with an\n  explicit `# shell-lint: allow-nonfatal` marker and a reason.\n\nShellCheck does not cover this — an `else` that only echoes is valid\nbash, so judging it needs repo-specific intent.\nEOF"
