propagate.                                                                                                                         |\n79:| F14 | Concurrency polarity is the inverse of the template's, with no compensating non-cancellable `main-writer` group → a rapid second push to main can cancel an in-flight publish.                                                                                                |\n80:| F15 | `npm warn allow-scripts` × 7 — `@sentry/node-cpu-profiler` postinstall never runs, so the native profiler binary is never built. Silent degradation.                                                                                                                          |\n81:| F16 | git `init.defaultBranch` hint × 14 blocks ≈ 98 log lines. The template silences this with workflow-level `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/KEY_0/VALUE_0`; hive-mind does not set it.                                                                                                         |\n82:| F17 | `DEP0040` punycode × 14, `DEP0005` Buffer × 2 — transitive/upstream, suppressible via `NODE_OPTIONS=--no-deprecation`.                                                                                                                                                        |\n83:| F18 | `npm warn using --force` × 4 — vestigial `--force` on the Playwright MCP global install (`Dockerfile:152`, `Dockerfile.dind:157`).                                                                                                                                            |\n84:| F19 | `warn: incorrect peer dependency \"solid-js@1.9.14\"` × 4 — upstream in `@link-assistant/agent`; only silenceable locally.                                                                                                                                                      |\n85:| F20 | `softprops/action-gh-release@v2` still targets Node 20, papered over by `FORCE_JAVASCRIPT_ACTIONS_TO_NODE24`. Actions are on `@v5`; template is on `@v6`.                                                                                                                     |\n100:   scripts to `.mjs` silently dropped `set -euo pipefail` semantics. Causes F1 and F4.\n104:   control falls through to success. Causes F3 and `release.yml:359,369`.\n105:3. **Verification granularity too coarse.** F5 retries the whole publish when only the\n110:1. **F1** — add strict exit-code checking to `helm-release.mjs`; publish from a `git\n113:2. **F5** — split retry granularity: poll `isVersionPublished` with backoff instead of\n115:3. **F4** — port the template's `push-main-with-rebase-retry.sh`; assert exit codes.\n117:5. **F6** — `timeout-minutes` on every job in both workflows; port\n119:6. **F3** — convert advisory `else` branches to `exit 1`; keep `|| true` only where a\n123:9. **F13/F14** — `always()` → `!cancelled()`; adopt the template's concurrency arrangement.\n136:- port `tests/ci-timeouts.test.js` (catches F6 forever);\n138:  synthetic `needs` contexts (catches F13);\n140:  F1/F4 class at source) — this is the highest-leverage single addition.\n144:The template is **not** vulnerable to F1 (it has no Helm release path) and is ahead of\n145:hive-mind on F3/F6/F9/F13/F14. One report is warranted in the opposite direction:\n154:Also worth filing, pending confirmation against the template's own logs: F5's\n162:is the Helm path: the fix for F1 should log each git command's exit code and assert the",
