[2026-07-19T13:21:21.128Z] [INFO]         "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent:**\n\n   There has been exactly **one** genuine user message in this entire task (the initial prompt). Every subsequent item has been an automated background-task notification or system-reminder, explicitly flagged as NOT user input and NOT approval. No user feedback or correction has ever been received.\n\n   The user is operating an AI issue solver on:\n   - **Repo/working dir:** `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784463865325` (link-assistant/hive-mind)\n   - **Branch (push ONLY to this):** `issue-2082-90c17c1e7d2a`\n   - **Issue:** https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2082 — *\"Check for all false positives, false negatives, warnings and errors in CI/CD and fix them all\"*\n   - **PR (already exists — update via `gh pr edit`, do NOT create new):** https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/2083\n\n   Explicit deliverables from the user message:\n   1. \"Download all logs and collect data related about the issue to this repository, and compile that data into the `./dev/log/issues/2082/pulls/2083` folder.\"\n   2. \"Use the collected evidence to do a deep analysis (search online for additional facts and data), reconstruct the timeline/sequence of events, list each and every requirement from the issue, find the root cause of each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement. Also check online for known existing components/libraries that solve a similar problem or can help.\"\n   3. \"If there is not enough data to find the actual root cause, add debug output and a verbose mode (if not already present) so the root cause can be found on the next iteration. Keep the default state switched off.\"\n   4. \"If the issue is related to another repository/project, report issues on GitHub for that project when possible. Each report must contain reproducible examples, workarounds, and suggestions for fixing the issue in code.\"\n   5. \"Double-check that the requirements are fully applied to the entire codebase: if an issue exists in multiple places, apply it in all of them.\"\n   6. \"Proceed.\"\n\n   Requirements derived from issue #2082 itself:\n   - **R1** Find & fix all CI/CD **false positives** (green checks verifying nothing)\n   - **R2** Find & fix all CI/CD **false negatives** (real failures reported as success)\n   - **R3** Find & fix all CI/CD **warnings**\n   - **R4** Find & fix all CI/CD **errors**\n   - **R5** Compare the **full file tree** against `https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template` and reuse all best practices\n   - **R6** \"if the same issue is found in template report issue also in templates\" → file upstream issues\n   - **R7** Follow `docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md`\n   - **R8** \"plan and execute everything in this single pull request … until it is each and every requirement fully addressed\"\n\n   Standing operational constraints from the user message (must persist): commit atomic steps to the branch; **create reproducing tests BEFORE fixes**; keep debug/experiment scripts in `./experiments` and real-world use cases in `./examples`; save large command output to files; run local CI checks (lint etc.) before pushing; download CI logs to `ci-logs/` and Read them; use `gh pr edit` to update PR 2083 and `gh pr ready 2083` when finished; verify clean `git status` at the end; merge default branch into the PR branch; check all three GitHub comment API endpoints (`/pulls/N/comments`, `/issues/N/comments`, `/pulls/N/reviews`) with `--paginate`.\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts:**\n   - **`command-stream`'s `\n\n**: fail-soft — resolves with `.code` instead of throwing. THE root-cause mechanism for F1 and F4; makes wrapping try/catch decorative.\n   - **`set -euo pipefail`** semantics restored in JS via a `runStrict` wrapper over `node:child_process.spawn`.\n   - **Mutation testing as validation**: after every fix, re-introduce the defect and confirm the new test fails with the expected message. Applied to F1, F5, F4 (×2), and F3.\n   - **YAML `!` is a tag sigil**: `if: !cancelled() && ...` is a *parse error*. GitHub Actions conditions starting with `!` must be wrapped in `${{ ... }}`. Block scalars (`if: |`) are literal text and need no wrapping. The previous `always()` spelling never needed this — which is exactly why the trap is easy to walk into.\n   - **GitHub Actions `timeout-minutes`**: absent → inherits the 360-minute default. **Not supported on jobs that call a reusable workflow via `uses:`** (job-level), while a *step-level* `uses:` is an action and does NOT exempt the job. Neither zizmor (#1023) nor actionlint (#49) enforces this — both open.\n   - **`always()` vs `!cancelled()`**: `always()` is true even after cancellation, defeating `cancel-in-progress`. `!cancelled()` expresses the real intent (run regardless of dependency results, but stop on cancellation).\n   - **Concurrency polarity**: cancelling a run on the publishing branch can interrupt it between `npm publish` and the version-bump `git push`, leaving the registry ahead of the repo — the same split-brain state as F4/F5.\n   - **Gate masking (newly discovered)**: every downstream job in `release.yml` is gated on `needs.changeset-check.result == 'success'`, so a missing changeset causes ALL other jobs to be **skipped**, hiding real regressions behind one red check.\n   - **npm registry CDN propagation lag** → E404 immediately after a successful publish (npm/cli#3424, #9043, #593); plus the **npm ≥11.5.1 OIDC Trusted-Publishing 404 red herring**.\n   - **npm `EPUBLISHCONFLICT`** — reported with a 403, so it must be classified *before* the non-retryable auth classifier.\n   - **js-yaml is only a transitive dependency** — not safe to depend on in checks that must survive an unknown `node_modules` state; hence hand-rolled line scanners in `scripts/*-lint.lib.mjs`, cross-validated against a real js-yaml parse.\n   - **ShellCheck does not cover vacuous assertions** — an `else` that only echoes is valid bash; judging it requires repo-specific intent.\n   - `use-m` dynamic package loading, `lino-arguments` config, `@hive-mind-test-suite default` annotation, ESLint flat config, lint-staged + prettier pre-commit hook.\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections:**\n\n   **Committed this session — `5b9155c7` (F3):**\n\n   - **`scripts/shell-lint.lib.mjs`** — CREATED. Detects `else` branches that report a failure without failing. Key constants and the nesting-aware collector:\n     ```js\n     const FAILURE_PHRASES = [/\\bcould not\\b/i, /\\bcouldn't\\b/i, /\\bnot found\\b/i, /\\bnot verif/i, /\\bunable to\\b/i, /\\bmissing\\b/i, /\\bfailed\\b/i, /\\bunexpected\\b/i];\n     const PROPAGATES_FAILURE = /(^|[\\s;&|(])(exit\\s+[1-9]|return\\s+[1-9]|false)(\\s|;|$)/m;\n     const RECORDS_FAILURE = /^\\s*[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*(\\+?=)/m;\n     const ALLOW_MARKER = /#\\s*shell-lint:\\s*allow-nonfatal\\b/;\n\n     export function findVacuousChecks(script) {\n       const lines = String(script || '').split('\\n');\n       const offenders = [];\n       for (let index = 0; index < lines.length; index++) {\n         if (!/^\\s*else\\s*(#.*)?$/.test(lines[index])) continue;\n         if (ALLOW_MARKER.test(lines[index])) continue;\n         // Only lines at the branch's OWN nesting level; a nested if's `exit 1`\n         // answers its own condition and must not launder the outer branch.\n         const body = [];\n         let depth = 0;\n         for (let cursor = index + 1; cursor < lines.length; cursor++) {\n           const line = lines[cursor];\n           if (/^\\s*if\\s/.test(line)) { depth++; continue; }\n           if (/^\\s*fi\\s*(#.*)?$/.test(line)) { if (depth === 0) break; depth--; continue; }\n           if (depth === 0) body.push(line);\n         }\n         const text = body.join('\\n');\n         if (PROPAGATES_FAILURE.test(text) || RECORDS_FAILURE.test(text) || ALLOW_MARKER.test(text)) continue;\n         const reported = body.find(line => FAILURE_PHRASES.some(phrase => phrase.test(line)));\n         if (reported) offenders.push({ line: index + 1, message: reported.trim() });\n       }\n       return offenders;\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`tests/shell-script-assertions-2082.test.mjs`** — CREATED. Header documents the ~32s-vs-`timeout 10s` root cause. 5 unit blocks (the exact shipped shape flagged at line 3; `exit 1` branch not flagged; alternative-outcome branch not flagged; accumulator branch not flagged; marked branch allowed AND the same branch flagged once the marker is stripped; nesting) + a repo sweep over `scripts/*.sh` with anti-vacuity guard `assert.ok(files.length > 0, ...)`.\n\n   - **`scripts/test-auto-fork-option.sh`** — REWRITTEN. Key additions:\n     ```bash\n     # The dry-run checks below exercise the real CLI, which makes several GitHub API\n     # calls before it reaches the auto-fork decision. Measured at ~32s; allow 3x.\n     DRY_RUN_TIMEOUT=\"${DRY_RUN_TIMEOUT:-120s}\"\n     failed=0\n     assert_log_matches() {\n       local description=\"$1\" pattern=\"$2\" logfile=\"$3\"\n       if grep -qE \"$pattern\" \"$logfile\"; then\n         echo \"PASS: $description\"\n       else\n         echo \"FAIL: $description\"\n         echo \"  expected output matching: $pattern\"\n         echo \"  ---- last 20 lines of $logfile ----\"\n         tail -20 \"$logfile\" | sed 's/^/  /'\n         echo \"  ----------------------------------\"\n         failed=1\n       fi\n     }\n     ```\n     Plus hermetic `--help` checks (`timeout 60s ./src/solve.mjs --help >solve_help.log 2>&1`), the three original dry-run checks now using `$DRY_RUN_TIMEOUT`, an explicit `Unknown option` check, and a terminating `if [ \"$failed\" -ne 0 ]; then echo \"--auto-fork option tests FAILED\"; exit 1; fi`.\n\n   - **`scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh`** — the silent skip became an error:\n     ```bash\n     else\n       # $RELEASE_YML is committed to this repository, so it can only be absent if the\n       # checkout is wrong or the file was moved. Skipping with a warning would let the\n       # line-limit check silently verify nothing (issue #2082).\n       echo \"ERROR: $RELEASE_YML not found — the line-limit check cannot run\"\n       echo \"::error::$RELEASE_YML not found. Update RELEASE_YML in scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh if the workflow moved.\"\n       FAILURES+=(\"$RELEASE_YML\")\n     fi\n     ```\n\n   - **`scripts/verify-docker-image.sh`** — three `else` lines annotated:\n     - `else # shell-lint: allow-nonfatal — diagnostics for the ERROR raised below.` (opam/rocq)\n     - `else # shell-lint: allow-nonfatal — informational; no bun global package is required.`\n     - `else # shell-lint: allow-nonfatal — see the reasoning below.` (configure-claude PR tolerance)\n\n   **Committed this session — `9a1cbf48` (F13/F14 + line-limit repair + changeset):**\n\n   - **`.github/workflows/release.yml`** — concurrency block rewritten:\n     ```yaml\n     # Concurrency: Only one workflow run per branch at a time.\n     # - main (releases): QUEUE. A run on main publishes to npm and then pushes the\n     #   version bump back to main. Cancelling it in between leaves the registry ahead\n     #   of the repository — the same split-brain state as issues #2082/F4 and #2082/F5,\n     #   reached by a different route. A newer release waits; it is never lost.\n     # - Other branches: CANCEL. Nothing is published from a PR run, so a superseded\n     #   run is only spending runners.\n     # This is the inverse of the original policy, which cancelled on main and queued\n     # everywhere else. See tests/ci-workflow-cancellation-2082.test.mjs.\n     #\n     # IMPORTANT: jobs must use !cancelled() rather than always() in `if:`, or they keep\n     # running after a cancellation and defeat the policy above. Enforced by the same test.\n     # See: docs/case-studies/issue-1274/README.md and docs/case-studies/issue-1278/README.md\n     concurrency:\n       group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}\n       cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.ref != 'refs/heads/main' }}\n     ```\n     Nine job conditions changed: 4 block-scalar cases had the redundant `      always() &&\\n      !cancelled() &&\\n` collapsed to `      !cancelled() &&\\n`; 5 inline cases became `if: ${{ !cancelled() && ... }}`. Affected jobs (verified by YAML diff): `test-compilation`, `check-file-line-limits`, `test-suites`, `test-execution`, `memory-check-linux`, `validate-docs`, `docker-pr-check`, `helm-pr-check`, `release`. The 5 `# Use !cancelled() instead of always()` comments on the Docker jobs remain.\n\n   - **`scripts/workflow-lint.lib.mjs`** — EXTENDED. `WorkflowJob` gained `condition`; `findJobs` gained block-scalar `if:` parsing; two new exports:\n     ```js\n     export function findJobsUsingAlways(yaml) {\n       return findJobs(yaml).filter(job => /\\balways\\(\\)/.test(job.condition));\n     }\n\n     export function inspectConcurrency(yaml, releaseBranch = 'main') {\n       const match = String(yaml || '').match(/^concurrency:\\s*\\n(?: {2}.*\\n?)*/m);\n       if (!match) return { hasConcurrency: false, cancelInProgress: null, cancelsReleaseBranch: false };\n       const cancel = match[0].match(/^ {2}cancel-in-progress:\\s*(.+)$/m);\n       const cancelInProgress = cancel ? cancel[1].trim() : null;\n       const cancelsReleaseBranch = cancelInProgress === 'true' || new RegExp(`==\\\\s*'refs/heads/${releaseBranch}'`).test(cancelInProgress || '');\n       return { hasConcurrency: true, cancelInProgress, cancelsReleaseBranch };\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`tests/ci-workflow-cancellation-2082.test.mjs`** — CREATED. Blocks: inline + block-scalar `if:` parsing (asserts 3 jobs found, i.e. a multi-line `if:` doesn't swallow following jobs); `findJobsUsingAlways` returns `['inline','block']`; `inspectConcurrency` on inverted/correct/`true`/absent; and a repo sweep asserting no job uses `always()` and no workflow cancels main.\n\n   - **`scripts/docker-pr-build.sh`** — CREATED. Extracted from release.yml; `set -euo pipefail`; `IMAGE_NAME`/`DIND_IMAGE_NAME` env with defaults `konard/hive-mind` / `konard/hive-mind-dind`; derives `BOX_VERSION`/`BOX_DIND_VERSION` from the Dockerfiles; two `docker build --progress=plain ... | tee`; folds in the former \"Verify build completed without errors\" step (`grep -E 'unbound variable' ... && exit 1`).\n\n   - **`scripts/docker-pr-verify-containers.sh`** — CREATED. Runs `verify-docker-image.sh` inside both images (DinD with `--privileged`) plus `bash scripts/verify-dind-exec-defaults.sh \"${DIND_IMAGE_NAME}:test\"`.\n\n   - **`.changeset/olive-pans-shout.md`** — CREATED, `'@link-assistant/hive-mind': patch`, summarizing all CI fixes.\n\n   **Previously committed (earlier sessions):** `ba3c57a4` (`scripts/run-command.lib.mjs` with `CommandFailedError`/`runCommand`/`runStrict`/`isVerbose` reading `HIVE_MIND_CI_VERBOSE`, `scripts/helm-release.lib.mjs`, `tests/helm-release-2082.test.mjs`, `dev/log/issues/2082/pulls/2083/README.md`, `analysis/F0-existing-solutions-research.md`, `.gitattributes`); `02498ca3` (F5: `isVersionConflict`, `waitForVersionOnRegistry`, `tests/publish-verification-race-2082.test.mjs`); `ec858696` (F4: `scripts/version-and-commit.lib.mjs` with `isNonFastForward`/`pushWithRebaseRetry`/`versionAndCommit`, thin CLI `version-and-commit.mjs`, `tests/version-and-commit-2082.test.mjs`); `0e4eb599` (F6: `scripts/workflow-lint.lib.mjs`, `tests/ci-workflow-timeouts-2082.test.mjs`, 22 `timeout-minutes` added).\n\n4. **Errors and fixes:**\n   - **Nesting bug in my own scanner** — `tests/shell-script-assertions-2082.test.mjs` failed `0 !== 1` because the branch collector swept in nested if-blocks, so an inner `exit 1` laundered the outer branch. Fixed by collecting only `depth === 0` lines.\n   - **Over-broad scanner (triage, not a bug)** — the repo sweep surfaced 9 hits including legitimate accumulator patterns and deliberate diagnostics. Rather than weaken the check, I added `RECORDS_FAILURE` (accumulators are genuinely correct) and an explicit `# shell-lint: allow-nonfatal` opt-out that must carry a reason, with a test asserting the same branch IS flagged once the marker is stripped.\n   - **Leftover garbage line** — `assert_log_matches \"...\" -- \"solve_help.log\"` survived my Write of `test-auto-fork-option.sh`; removed by Edit.\n   - **YAML tag parse failure (significant)** — bulk-replacing `if: always() && ` with `if: !cancelled() && ` produced `PARSE FAILED: unknown tag !<!cancelled()> (156:264)`. Fixed with a second pass wrapping those 5 inline conditions in `${{ ... }}`; block-scalar cases needed nothing. Re-verified `PARSE OK, jobs: 25`.\n   - **Self-inflicted line-limit regression (significant)** — my own F6 commit `0e4eb599` pushed `release.yml` from 1491 → 1512 lines, breaking `check-file-line-limits.sh`. Fixed by extracting two Docker scripts (1514 → 1452).\n   - **Why CI never caught it** — investigated per protocol: all 4 pushed commits showed `failure`, but the ONLY failing job was `Check for Changesets`; `check-file-line-limits` and everything else were **skipped**, because all downstream jobs are gated on `needs.changeset-check.result == 'success'`. Adding the changeset unblocked the real suite.\n   - **Mutation-check false reassurance (prior session, carried forward)** — a too-narrow `grep -E \"AssertionError\"` made a caught mutant look uncaught; always re-run without the grep.\n   - **`jq` unavailable (exit 127)** — continue using `gh --jq`, `node -e`, and `python3`.\n   - **Shell cwd persistence (prior session)** — always prefix with the absolute `cd /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784463865325`.\n   - No user corrections have ever been received — only one user turn exists.\n\n5. **Problem Solving:**\n\n   **F3 — SOLVED, TESTED (reproduced first), MUTATION-VALIDATED, COMMITTED `5b9155c7`, PUSHED.** Root cause is *two* compounding defects: the assertion branches printed \"Could not verify …\" and fell through to `exit 0`, AND the `timeout 10s` was far too short — measured 32.6s for the `Auto-fork:` marker to appear, because solve.mjs makes several GitHub API calls first. So both greps had been failing on every run while the job stayed green. The rewritten script passes all 5 assertions end-to-end (EXIT=0); the mutation `DRY_RUN_TIMEOUT=10s` reproduces the production failure as EXIT=1 with exactly those two checks red. Generalized via `shell-lint.lib.mjs` so the pattern cannot return anywhere in `scripts/*.sh`.\n\n   **F13/F14 — SOLVED, TESTED (reproduced first), COMMITTED `9a1cbf48`, PUSHED.** F14: the concurrency policy was inverted, cancelling runs on the only branch that publishes. F13: 9 jobs used `always()`, defeating cancellation, contradicting release.yml's own documented rule which had only ever been applied to the Docker jobs. Semantics verified by a real YAML parse diff: exactly 9 of 25 jobs changed, each only in the leading term.\n\n   **Line-limit repair + changeset** — restored `release.yml` to 1452 lines and unblocked the CI gate that had been masking every other job.\n\n   **CI status (in progress at cutoff):** run `29688553362` for `9a1cbf48` — `Check for Changesets`, `Check for Manual Version Changes`, `check-file-line-limits`, `detect-changes`, `helm-pr-check`, `validate-docs` all **success**; `lint` and `test-compilation` still running. This is the first run in which the full suite actually executes.\n\n   **Background agent `a48b7675bdca78e23` (tests/ ESLint cleanup, F21) is STILL RUNNING** with uncommitted changes to `eslint.config.mjs` and ~20 `tests/*.mjs` files. Its output file is JSONL. I have staged only my own files by explicit path in every `git add`, so all commits stayed clean.\n\n6. **All user messages:**\n\n   There has been exactly **one** user message — the initial task prompt. Its verbatim key constraints:\n   - \"Download all logs and collect data related about the issue to this repository, and compile that data into the ./dev/log/issues/2082/pulls/2083 folder.\"\n   - \"Use the collected evidence to do a deep analysis (search online for additional facts and data), reconstruct the timeline/sequence of events, list each and every requirement from the issue, find the root cause of each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement. Also check online for known existing components/libraries that solve a similar problem or can help.\"\n   - \"If there is not enough data to find the actual root cause, add debug output and a verbose mode (if not already present) so the root cause can be found on the next iteration. Keep the default state switched off.\"\n   - \"If the issue is related to another repository/project, report issues on GitHub for that project when possible. Each report must contain reproducible examples, workarounds, and suggestions for fixing the issue in code.\"\n   - \"Double-check that the requirements are fully applied to the entire codebase: if an issue exists in multiple places, apply it in all of them.\"\n   - \"Proceed.\"\n\n   No further user messages have been received. All subsequent transcript items were automated `<task-notification>` / `<system-reminder>` events, each explicitly stating they are NOT user input and must NOT be treated as approval or consent.\n\n7. **Pending Tasks:**\n   1. **Confirm CI run `29688553362` goes green** — `lint` and `test-compilation` were still in flight at cutoff. If red, download logs to `ci-logs/` and Read them.\n   2. **F7** — split the four files at exactly 1500 lines (`src/solve.mjs`, `src/claude.lib.mjs`, `src/codex.lib.mjs`, `src/telegram-solve-queue.lib.mjs`). Note `tests/test-interactive-mode.mjs` also appeared in the warn list.\n   3. **F3 remainder** — `scripts/test-global-commands.sh` still has `|| true` on `hive --version` / `solve --version` / `--help` followed by unconditional \"works\" claims; and `release.yml:359,369` has the same inline shape. (The `npm unlink -g … || true` trap-cleanup lines should be left alone.) `scripts/verify-log-file-contents.sh` was inspected and is already correct.\n   4. **F8** — `check-mjs-syntax.sh` to cover `scripts/`, add the missing `timeout 10s` on the tests loop.\n   5. **F9** — add `.secretlintrc.json` + CI step.\n   6. **F10** — `npm pkg fix` for the `bin` `./` prefixes.\n   7. **F11** — remove the Sentry sourcemap step (meaningless with no build step).\n   8. **F12/F15–F20** — jscpd ignores + threshold, `allowScripts` decision, `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/KEY_0/VALUE_0`, `NODE_OPTIONS=--no-deprecation`, drop `--force` from Dockerfiles, bump actions `@v5`→`@v6`.\n   9. **F21** — tests/ ESLint coverage (delegated to the still-running background agent; needs review + commit when it reports).\n   10. **F5 follow-up** — check the publish job's npm version against the ≥11.5.1 OIDC-404 caveat.\n   11. **R7 docs** — add timeout + cancellation sections to `docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md` and its `zh`/`hi`/`ru` translations.\n   12. **R6 upstream** — file issue(s) on `link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template` with reproducible example + workaround + suggested code fix.\n   13. **Analysis docs** — add write-ups for F4, F5, F6, F13/F14 to `dev/log/issues/2082/pulls/2083/analysis/` (F0–F3 exist); update the master README's solution-plan checkboxes for F1/F3/F4/F5/F6/F13/F14 now done. Consider documenting the newly discovered gate-masking effect.\n   14. Merge `main` into the branch; run full local CI; update PR 2083 via `gh pr edit`; verify CI green; `gh pr ready 2083`; confirm clean `git status`.\n\n8. **Current Work:**\n\n   I had just committed and pushed `9a1cbf48` (\"fix(ci): stop cancelling releases mid-publish, drop always() (#2082)\") and was **monitoring CI run `29688553362`** — the first run where the changeset gate passes and the real suite executes. The most recent command was:\n\n   ```\n   gh run view 29688553362 --json jobs --jq '.jobs[]|select(.conclusion!=\"skipped\")|\"\\(.conclusion // .status)  \\(.name)\"' | sort\n   ```\n\n   which returned:\n   ```\n     lint\n     test-compilation\n   success  Check for Changesets\n   success  Check for Manual Version Changes\n   success  check-file-line-limits\n   success  detect-changes\n   success  helm-pr-check\n   success  validate-docs\n   ```\n\n   `lint` and `test-compilation` have blank conclusions (still running). Six jobs are green, including `check-file-line-limits` — confirming the 1452-line release.yml repair landed correctly.\n\n   Immediately before starting the CI wait, I had begun the analysis-doc deliverable, listing `dev/log/issues/2082/pulls/2083/analysis/` (contains `F0-existing-solutions-research.md`, `F1-helm-release-false-negative.md`, `F2-template-gap-analysis.md`, `F3-vacuous-tests-false-positives.md`, plus log excerpts) and grepping the master README's findings table and solution plan.\n\n9. **Optional Next Step:**\n\n   Finish polling CI run `29688553362` until `lint` and `test-compilation` conclude, and if either fails, follow the user's investigation protocol — \"Step 3: For each non-passing run, download logs to preserve them: `gh run view {run-id} --repo link-assistant/hive-mind --log > ci-logs/{workflow}-{run-id}.log`\" and Read them.\n\n   Once CI is confirmed, resume the analysis-log deliverable I had just started — the user's explicit request to \"compile that data into the `./dev/log/issues/2082/pulls/2083` folder\" and \"find the root cause of each problem\" — by adding write-ups for the findings closed since F3 (F4, F5, F6, F13/F14) and updating the master README's solution-plan checkboxes, which currently still read as open:\n\n   > `110:1. **F1** — add strict exit-code checking to helm-release.mjs …`\n   > `123:9. **F13/F14** — always() → !cancelled(); adopt the template's concurrency arrangement.`\n\n   The gate-masking discovery is worth recording there too,