[2026-07-19T13:39:49.149Z] [INFO]       {
[2026-07-19T13:39:49.149Z] [INFO]         "type": "text",
[2026-07-19T13:39:49.149Z] [INFO]         "text": "CI run [29688858773](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/actions/runs/29688858773) is **green** — all 10 executed jobs pass.\n\n**Where things stand:**\n\nThe previous run surfaced two genuine failures, both caused by my own release.yml extraction: `tests/test-docker-release-order.mjs` and `tests/test-docker-dind-variant.mjs` asserted on the literal `docker build --progress=plain` text being *inline* in the workflow. I'd moved it into `scripts/docker-pr-build.sh`.\n\nI fixed those by making the tests follow the indirection rather than deleting the assertions — the job must invoke each script **and** each script must still contain the build/verify commands. Mutation-checked: stubbing out `docker-pr-build.sh` makes both tests fail, so they'd catch an empty script rather than just a present filename. Committed as `740cfe98`.\n\n**One gap I want to flag rather than paper over:** `docker-pr-check` was *skipped* in this run — commit `740cfe98` touched only tests and docs, so the path filter didn't trigger it. That means the two scripts I extracted (`docker-pr-build.sh`, `docker-pr-verify-containers.sh`) have **still never actually executed in CI**; in the run where `docker-pr-check` did fire, it died at the first step (the static contract test) before reaching them. The static assertions pass locally, but \"the extracted build actually builds\" is currently unverified. Upcoming fixes touch `release.yml`, which will trigger the job naturally — I'll confirm it there rather than assume.\n\nAlso worth noting: the local `npm run test` run I did is not usable as evidence. It stopped at `tests/test-hive-screens.mjs` (exit 13), but the background ESLint agent was rewriting that exact file mid-run; it passes standalone. CI on a clean checkout is the authority here.\n\nI also wrote `dev/log/issues/2082/pulls/2083/analysis/implementation-log.md`, recording root cause + fix + mutation check for F1/F3/F4/F5/F6/F13/F14, including the gate-masking effect: because nearly every job is gated on `needs.changeset-check.result == 'success'`, a missing changeset skipped the entire suite — which is why my own 1500-line-limit break reached the branch unnoticed. That's a structural false negative in its own right and belongs in the findings list.\n\nNext: F7 (splitting the four 1500-line files), the F3 remainder in `test-global-commands.sh` and `release.yml:359,369`, then the smaller F8–F20 items."
